hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6601","756 - With the same chain of transmission, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever owes a debt, let him repay it or seek release from it before he repays it on a Day when there is neither gold nor silver. They said: With what will he repay, O Messenger of Allah? He said: It will be taken from his good deeds; if they suffice, otherwise the sins of the other person will be cast upon him."
"6602","757 - With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three at whom Allah will not look on the Day of Resurrection: the aged adulterer, the lying ruler, and the destitute arrogant one."
"6603","758 - With the same chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when he prayed over the funeral, he said: O Allah, Your servant and the son of Your servant, he used to testify that there is no god but You and that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger, and You know him best; if he was a doer of good, increase him in his goodness, and if he was an evildoer, forgive him; do not deprive us of his reward, and do not test us after him."
"6604","759 - With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Richness is not from abundance of goods; richness is only richness of the soul."
"6605","760 - With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, Allah is more joyful at the repentance of His servant than one of you is at finding his lost animal in the desert."
"6606","761 - With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, meaning Allah Almighty said: When My servant draws near to Me a handspan, I draw near to him a cubit; when he draws near to Me a cubit, I draw near to him a fathom; and when he draws near to Me a fathom, I come to him hastening."
"6607","762 - With the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, whoever fights in the path of Allah, will he enter Paradise? He said: Yes. He waited a little, as if he had heard something, then said: Where is the one who asked just now? The man stood up, and he said: What did you say? He said: I said: Tell me, whoever strives in the path of Allah and is killed, will he enter Paradise? You said: Yes. He said: Then he said: Gabriel has informed me of that, except if he owes a debt."
"6608","763 - With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not sit in the roadways nor in the courtyards. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we cannot avoid that. He said: If not, then give them their due right. They said: O Prophet of Allah, what is their right? He said: Returning the greeting, lowering the gaze, responding to the sneezer, and guiding the way."
"6609","764 - Abu Mamar Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Said, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is overcome by vomiting, there is no make-up upon him, and whoever induces vomiting, upon him is the make-up."
"6610","765 - Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, who said: We saw Abu Hurayrah performing ablution on the roof of the mosque, so I said: O Abu Hurayrah, for what are you performing ablution? He said: I ate a piece of dried cheese; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Perform ablution from what fire has altered."
"6611","766 - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Dawud al-Attar narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Said ibn Abi Said, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This wealth is green and sweet; whoever takes it rightly, it will be blessed for him in it; and many a one who plunges into the wealth of Allah and His Messenger for what his soul desires, for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"6612","767 - Al-Hasan ibn Arafah al-Abdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ibrahim al-Ghifari narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam, from Said ibn Abi Said, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was taken up to the lowest heaven, and I did not pass a heaven but I found in it my name: Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, and Abu Bakr al-Siddiq behind me."
"6613","768 - Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Said ibn Abi Said, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When the slave-girl of one of you commits adultery and her adultery becomes clear, let him flog her and not rebuke her; then if she commits adultery, let him flog her the prescribed punishment and not rebuke her - Sufyan said: meaning, not disgrace her - then if she commits adultery, let him flog her the prescribed punishment and not rebuke her; then if she commits adultery, let him sell her even for a rope of hair."
"6614","769 - Dawud ibn Amr narrated to us, Hibban ibn Ali narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Said, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rikaz is gold that grows out of the earth."
"6615","770 - Dawud ibn Amr narrated to us, Hibban ibn Ali al-Anazi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you buys a servant, let him take her forelock and say: O Allah, I ask You for her good and the good of what You fashioned her upon; and when he buys a camel, let him take the top of its hump and say the like of that."
"6616","771 - Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Said narrated to us, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the son of Adam had two valleys of gold, he would wish for a third to add to them, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust."
"6617","772 - Ibrahim ibn Said narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Fadl, from Said ibn Abi Said, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a leaning wall and hastened, and said: I dislike sudden death."
"6618","773 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Safwan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind, from Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Akhnasi, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is made a judge among the people has been slaughtered without a knife."
"6619","774 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, who said: I heard my father and Said narrating from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no commander over ten except he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection shackled; justice will free him or injustice will destroy him."
"6620","775 - Sufyan ibn Waki narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Yahya ibn Umayr al-Madini narrated to us, who said: I heard Said al-Maqburi say: Abu Hurayrah led us in prayer, and he used to say takbir whenever he rose and prostrated; when he finished, he said: This is how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray with us."
"6621","776 - Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Sufyan and Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a dinar. He said: Spend it on yourself. He said: I have another dinar. He said: Spend it on your wife. He said: I have another dinar. He said: Spend it on your child. He said: I have another dinar. He said: Spend it on your servant. He said: I have another dinar. He said: You know best."
"6622","777 - Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, who said: Said ibn Abi Said informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I intended to command the tooth-stick along with ablution, and to delay the prayer to the middle of the night, or to a third of the night."
"6623","778 - Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, who said: Ibrahim ibn al-Fadl al-Makhzumi narrated to me, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ward off the prescribed punishments as much as you can."
"6624","779 - Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Ishaq, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been permitted to narrate about an angel whose feet have pierced the seventh earth, with the Throne on his shoulder, saying: Glory be to You, where You were and where You will be."
"6625","780 - Ibrahim ibn Ararah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Man narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased that his lifetime be extended for him and his provision be expanded for him, let him uphold his kinship ties."
"6626","781 - Ahmad ibn Imran al-Akhnasi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Umarah ibn al-Qaqa narrated to us, from Abu Zurah, who said: I entered the house of Marwan with Abu Hurayrah, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: That... and who is more unjust than one who creates a creation... the hadith."
"6627","782 - Ubaydullah al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, who said: Said ibn Abi Said narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man entered the mosque while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the mosque; he prayed, then came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Go back and pray, for you have not prayed. He repeated that three times. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I do not know better than this, so teach me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: When you intend to pray, say takbir, then recite what is easy for you of the Quran, then bow until you are tranquil while bowing, then rise until you stand upright, then prostrate until you are tranquil while prostrating, then rise until you sit evenly, then do in all your prayer likewise."
"6628","783 - Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, who said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to me, who said: Ali ibn Yahya ibn Khallad narrated to me, from his father, from his uncle - and he had witnessed Badr - who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque when a man entered and prayed; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept watching him. He prayed, then came to the Messenger of Allah and greeted him; the Messenger of Allah returned the greeting, then said: Go back and pray, for you have not prayed. He went back and prayed, then came to the Messenger of Allah and greeted him; the Messenger of Allah returned the greeting, then said: Go back and pray, for you have not prayed. He did that two or three times, then said to him the second or third time: O Messenger of Allah, I have exhausted myself, so teach me and show me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: When you intend to pray, perform ablution and perfect your ablution, then face the qiblah and say takbir, then recite, then bow until you are tranquil while bowing, then rise until you stand evenly, then prostrate until you are tranquil while prostrating, then rise until you are tranquil while sitting, then prostrate until you are tranquil while prostrating, then rise until you are tranquil while sitting; if you complete your prayer upon this, you have completed it, and whatever you omit of that, you only omit it from your prayer."
"6629","784 - Abu Said al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, Said al-Maqburi narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, that Ammar ibn Yasir prayed two rakahs and shortened them. Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith said to him: O Abu al-Yaqzan, I see you shortened them. He said: I hastened with them against whispering, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man prays the prayer and perhaps there is for him of it only a tenth, or a ninth, or an eighth, or a seventh, or a sixth, until he went through the number."
"6630","785 - Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muammal narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, who said: Said al-Maqburi informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: We set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of Tabuk; we stopped at Thaniyyat al-Wada. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw lamps and saw women weeping. He said: What is this? It was said: They were granted temporary marriage and they are weeping. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Marriage, divorce, waiting period, and inheritance have forbidden - or he said: demolished - temporary marriage."
"6631","786 - Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Jushami narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sitting in the courtyards and roadways. The Muslims said to him: We cannot avoid that. He said: If not, then give them their right. They said: What is their right? He said: Returning the greeting, responding to the sneezer when he praises Allah Almighty, lowering the gaze, and guiding the way."
"6632","787 - With the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah loves sneezing and dislikes yawning; when one of you yawns, let him not say ah ah, for Satan laughs at him and plays with him."
"6633","788 - With the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Two men sat with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), one of them nobler than the other; the noble one sneezed and did not praise Allah, so he did not respond to him, while the other sneezed and praised Allah, so he responded to him."
"6634","789 - Amr ibn al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no commander over ten except he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection shackled until justice frees him or injustice destroys him."
"6635","790 - Al-Ashajj narrated to us, Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining of a neighbor of his. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said three times: Be patient. Then he said to him the fourth or third time: Put your goods in the road. He said: People began passing by him and saying: What is wrong with you? He said: His neighbor harmed him, so they began saying: May Allah curse him. Then his neighbor came and said: Take back your goods, and I will never harm you again."
"6636","791 - Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Said narrated to us, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: How will you be when you collect neither dinar nor dirham? They said: Do you see that happening? He said: Yes, by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Abu Hurayrah, from the words of the Truthful, the Believed. They said: From what will this be? He said: The covenant of Allah and the covenant of His Messenger will be violated, so Allah will harden the hearts of the people of the covenant, and they will withhold what is in their hands."
"6637","792 - Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from al-Jurayri, from Mudarib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I said: Did you hear from your beloved a hadith you narrate? He said: Yes, I heard him say: No contagion, no omens, and the best of omens is the good omen; the evil eye is true; the cross is about to be broken, the pig killed, and the jizyah laid down."
"6638","793 - Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Khuthaym ibn Irak ibn Malik narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Grant respite for the sake of Allah, grant respite; for were it not for bowed old men, humble youth, suckling babes, and grazing beasts, punishment would be poured upon you in torrents."
"6639","794 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ashath ibn Barraz narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first of what will be lifted from this nation is modesty and trust, and the last of what remains of it is prayer; it appears to me he said: And a people may pray who have no share."
"6640","795 - Abdullah ibn Salamah al-Basri narrated to us, Ashath ibn Barraz narrated to us, from al-Hasan, who said: When this verse was revealed: You will surely be asked that Day about bliss, they said: O Messenger of Allah, about which bliss will we be asked? Our swords are on our shoulders. And he mentioned the hadith."
"6641","796 - Abdullah ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ashath ibn Barraz narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of this."
"6642","797 - Salih ibn Malik narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Abi al-Musawir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who performs ablution and perfects it, then walks to one of the houses of Allah to pray in it a prescribed prayer, except a good deed is written for him for every step, a sin is erased from him with the other, and he is raised by the other a degree."
"6643","798 - Salih ibn Malik narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Abi al-Musawir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no servant who falls ill with an illness except Allah commands his guardian angel: Whatever evil deed he did, do not write it; whatever good deed he did, write it for him as ten good deeds; and write for him righteous deeds as he used to do while healthy, even if he does not do them."
"6644","799 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Zakariyya, from al-Shabi, from Abu Hurayrah, raising the hadith, who said: The pledge is ridden and fed, and the milk of the milch animal is drunk, and upon the one who drinks it is the upkeep and feed."
"6645","800 - Zakariyya narrated to us, Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays over a funeral, for him is a qirat; and whoever waits until it is buried, for him are two qirats; the qirat is like Uhud."
"6646","801 - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Amir, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade marrying a woman over her paternal aunt, and the maternal aunt over her sister's daughter; the younger is not married over the elder, nor the elder over the younger."
"6647","802 - Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Talhah ibn Sinan al-Iyami narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Amir, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Adam met Moses, and he said to him: Are you Adam who brought people out of Paradise? The hadith."
"6648","803 - Abu Hammam narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, that Zakariyya informed them, from Amir, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the first to raise his head after the last blowing; then Moses will be clinging to the Throne, and I will not know whether he was like that or after the blowing."
"6649","804 - Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, that Abu al-Samh narrated to him, from Ibn Hujayrah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The believer in his grave is in a garden; his grave is widened for him seventy cubits and illuminated for him like the moon on the night of full moon. Do you see concerning what this verse was revealed: Then indeed for him is a straitened life, and We will gather him on the Day of Resurrection blind. He said: Do you know what the straitened life is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The punishment of the disbeliever in his grave; by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, ninety-nine dragons will be set upon them. Do you know what the dragon is? He said: Ninety-nine snakes, each snake having seven heads, blowing into his body, stinging him and scratching him until the Day of Resurrection."
"6650","805 - Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Ziyad ibn Qays, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near: knowledge will decrease and harj will increase. He said: I said: What is abundant harj, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Killing, killing."
"6651","806 - Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Isam ibn Taliq al-Basri narrated to us, from Shuayb ibn al-Ala, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A man was killed as a martyr in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). A weeping woman wept over him and said: O martyr! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hush! What makes you know he is a martyr? Perhaps he used to speak of what did not concern him, and be miserly with what would not decrease him."
"6652","807 - Hudbah narrated to us, Sallam ibn Miskin narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abdullah ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proceeded to Mecca to conquer it; he said to Abu Hurayrah: O Abu Hurayrah, call out to the Ansar. He said: O company of Ansar, answer the Messenger of Allah. They came as if they were upon an appointment. He said: Take this road, and let none appear to you except you put him to sleep, meaning: you kill him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marched, and Allah granted him victory. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated the House and prayed two rakahs, then came out from the door facing al-Safa, ascended al-Safa, and addressed the people while the Ansar were below him. Some of the Ansar said to one another: As for the man, tenderness for his people has seized him, and love for his town. Allah Almighty sent down revelation to him of what the Ansar said, and he said: O company of Ansar, you say: As for the man, tenderness for his people has seized him, and love for his town? Who am I then? Nay, by Allah, I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger; life is your life and death is your death. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we said that only fearing you would leave us. He said: You are truthful with Allah and with His Messenger. By Allah, there was none of them but wet his throat with tears from his eyes."
"6653","808 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Maqabiri narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, who said: Muhammad narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yaqub, freedman of al-Huraqah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lower garment of the believer is to the middle of the shins, and below that to above the ankles; whatever is below the ankles is in the Fire."
"6654","809 - Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah) distributed dates, and I received five dates and a dry one. He said: I found the dry one the hardest of them on my tooth."
"6655","809 (bis) - And Abu Hurayrah said: The most miserly of people is he who is miserly with greeting, and the most incapable of people is he who is incapable of supplication."
"6656","810 - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Uthman, that Abu Hurayrah was on a journey; when they stopped and the meal-spread was laid, they sent for him while he was praying. He said: I am fasting. When they were about to finish, he came and began eating. The people looked at their messenger, who said: What are you looking at? By Allah, he informed me he was fasting. Abu Hurayrah said: He spoke the truth; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever fasts three days of every month has fasted the whole lifetime; I have fasted three days of every month, so the whole month is mine; and I found its confirmation in the Book of Allah Almighty: Whoever comes with a good deed, for him are ten like it. And he recited it another time, saying: I have fasted three days from the beginning of the month, and I am breaking fast in the lightening of Allah, fasting in the multiplying of Allah Almighty."
"6657","811 - Sulayman ibn Abd al-Jabbar Abu Ayyub narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, from Abd al-Salam ibn Ajlan al-Hujaymi, Abu Uthman al-Nahdi narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the first for whom the gate of Paradise will be opened, except that a woman will hasten me; I will say to her: What is with you? And who are you? She will say: I am a woman who stayed to raise orphans of mine."
"6658","812 - Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Hurayrah who said: My intimate and beloved Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the owner of this chamber, said: Mercy is not removed except from a wretched one."
"6659","813 - Ubaydullah ibn Muadh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abbas al-Jurayri, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed seven dates among us; we were seven, and he gave us a date each."
"6660","814 - Abdullah ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, al-Qasim narrated to us, from Hisham, from Zayd ibn Aslam who said: He used to inform us from Dhakwan Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah Almighty created Adam, He wiped over his back, and there fell from his back every soul He will create until the Day of Resurrection; He placed between the eyes of every person of them a glimmer of light, then presented them to Adam. He said: O Lord, who are these? He said: These are your offspring. He saw a man among them and was pleased by the glimmer between his eyes, and said: O Lord, who is this? He said: A man from your offspring in the last of the nations called Dawud. He said: O Lord, how long did You make his life? He said: Sixty years. He said: Add to him forty years of my life. He said: Then it will be written and sealed and not changed. When the life of Adam, upon him be peace, ended and the Angel of Death came to him, he said: Has there not remained forty years of my life? He said: Did you not give them to your son Dawud? He denied, so his offspring denied; he forgot, so his offspring forgot; he erred, so his offspring erred."
"6661","815 - Shuja ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Marwan narrated to us, from Abu al-Malih al-Madani, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not ask Allah, He is angry with him."
"6662","816 - Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from Kamil Abu al-Ala, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lifespan of my nation is between sixty years and seventy."
"6663","817 - Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, from Malik, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umrah to umrah is expiation for what is between them, and the accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise."
"6664","818 - Ahmad ibn Isa al-Misri narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Sumayy, that he heard Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The closest the servant is to his Lord is while he is prostrating, so increase supplication."
"6665","819 - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever prays over a funeral, for him is a qirat; and whoever follows it until it is finished, for him are two qirats, the smaller of them - or one of them - like Uhud."
"6666","820 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Sumayy informed me, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise, and umrah to umrah - or the two umrahs - expiate what is between them."
"6667","821 - Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"6668","822 - Abu Khaythamah and Dawud ibn Amr narrated to us - Abu Yala said: I copied it from the copy of Abu Khaythamah - they said: Sufyan narrated to us, Sumayy narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge from the hardship of trial, the reaching of wretchedness, the evil of decree, and the gloating of enemies."
"6669","823 - Ishaq narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sneezed, he lowered his voice with it and covered his face."
"6670","824 - Muhammad ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Messenger of Allah, spreading the hands burdens us in prayer, so he commanded them to seek help with the knees."
"6671","825 - Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, who said: Al-Murajja ibn Raja al-Yashkuri narrated to us, Isa ibn Hilal narrated to us, from Bashir ibn Nuhayk who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: My beloved Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me, who said: The Hour will not come until there comes out against them a man from my household, and he will strike them until they return to the truth. He said: I said: How long will it be? He said: Five and two. He said: I said: What is five and two? He said: I do not know."
"6672","826 - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Uthman, that Abu Hurayrah was on a journey; when they stopped, the meal-spread was laid, they sat with him, and he mentioned the hadith."
"6673","827 - Jafar ibn Humayd narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Mamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man driving a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial animal. He said: Ride it. He said: I saw him keeping pace with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a sandal on its neck."
"6674","828 - Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, who said: Musa ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to me, meaning from al-Hakam ibn Aban, who said: Ikrimah narrated to me, who said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to me, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the pulpit mentioning the hour on Friday; I saw him clench his fingers and make them few."
"6675","829 - Ishaq narrated to us, Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Umayyah ibn Shibl, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrating about Moses, upon him be peace, on the pulpit. He said: It occurred in his mind: Does Allah Almighty sleep? So Allah sent him an angel who kept him awake three times, then gave him two flasks, a flask in each hand, and commanded him to guard them. He said: He began to sleep while his hands almost met, then wake and hold one over the other, until he slept a sleep and his hands struck together and the two flasks broke. He said: Allah struck for him a parable that if Allah Almighty slept, the heaven and earth would not hold together."
"6676","830 - Ishaq narrated to us, Abu Ubaydah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad, he is Ibn Shabib, from Jafar ibn Abi Wahshiyyah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: If there were in this mosque a hundred or more, and in it a man of the Fire, and he breathed and his breath reached them, the mosque and those in it would burn."
"6677","831 - Bishr ibn Sayhan narrated to us, Harb ibn Maymun narrated to us, Musa ibn Ubaydah al-Rabadhi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from Abu Hurayrah who said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with his hand in my hand; he came upon a man of shabby appearance. He said: Abu so-and-so? What has brought you to what I see? He said: Illness and harm, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Shall I not teach you words by which Allah will remove illness and harm from you? He said: No, I would not be pleased with them even if I had witnessed Badr and Uhud with you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed, then said: Do the people of Badr and Uhud attain what the contented poor one attains? He said: Abu Hurayrah said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me. He said: Say, O Abu Hurayrah: I rely upon the Living who does not die; praise be to Allah who has not taken a son, and has no partner in dominion, and has no protector out of weakness; and magnify Him greatly. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon me when my condition had improved, and said: What is the news? He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I kept saying the words you taught me."
"6678","832 - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ziyad al-Harithi, from Abu Hurayrah who said: A man said to him: Are you the one who forbids fasting on Friday? He said: No, by the Lord of this building - or this sanctuary - I did not forbid it; Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it."
"6679","833 - Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ulayy, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The women of Quraysh are the best women who rode camels: the most tender to a child in his smallness, and the most careful of a husband in what is in his hand. Abu Hurayrah said: We say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew that the daughter of Imran did not ride camels."
"6680","834 - Muhammad ibn Qudamah narrated to us, who said: I heard Sufyan say: Ismail narrated to us, from Qays who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: By Allah, for one of you to take a rope and gather firewood, carrying it on his back, eating and giving charity, is better for him than coming to a man whom Allah has enriched from His bounty and asking him, whether he gives or withholds."
"6681","835 - Muhammad ibn Qudamah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"6682","836 - Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Hatim narrated to us, from al-Harith, from his uncle, from Abu Hurayrah who said: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave me as I have left you, and do not ask me about anything; those before you were destroyed only by their many questions and their differing with their prophets. What I forbid you, avoid it; and what I command you, follow of it what you can."
"6683","837 - With the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you breathe into the vessel when drinking from it; but when he wants to drink from it, let him move it away, then breathe."
"6684","838 - With the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The purification of the vessel of one of you when the dog laps is to wash it seven times."
"6685","839 - Kamil ibn Talhah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar al-Umari narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you yawns, let him place his hand over his mouth, lest anything enter."
"6686","840 - Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Ubaydah narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until time draws near, and the year is like the month, the month like the Friday, the Friday like the day, and the day like the burning of a palm frond, meaning the palm leaf."
"6687","841 - Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hamzah ibn al-Mughirah, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not make my grave an idol; may Allah curse a people who took the graves of their prophets as mosques."
"6688","842 - Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give the worker his wage before his sweat dries."
"6689","843 - Al-Salt ibn Masud al-Jahdari narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Rabiah informed me, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged with an oath along with a witness."
"6690","844 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The gates of Paradise are opened every Monday and Thursday - Suhayl said in his hadith: So Allah forgives every servant who does not associate anything with Allah except the two estranged ones; Allah Almighty says to His angels: Leave them until they reconcile. Mamar said: Other than Suhayl said: And deeds are presented every Monday and Thursday."
"6691","845 - With the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah loves a servant, He says: O Gabriel, I love so-and-so, so love him. He said: Gabriel says to the people of heaven: Your Lord loves so-and-so, so love him; the people of heaven love him. He said: And acceptance is placed for him on earth. He said: And when He hates, the like of that."
"6692","846 - Amr ibn Husayn narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Ala narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you intends a journey, let him bid farewell to his brothers, for they add to his supplication with their supplication goodness."
"6693","847 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Asim, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does the deed of the people of Lut, stone the upper and the lower, stone them both together."
"6694","848 - Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed a man of his companions, then he met him and said: Why have I not seen you? He said: I did not sleep last night; a scorpion stung me. He said: Had you said when you entered evening: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He created, it would not have harmed you. Ubaydullah said: I do not know it but he said in the hadith, raising it: Whoever says it when he enters evening and when he enters morning, it will not harm him."
"6695","849 - Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, will we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection? He said: He said: Are you harmed in seeing the moon on the night of full moon with no cloud beneath it? They said: No. He said: Are you harmed in seeing the sun at noon with no cloud beneath it? They said: No. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, you will surely see Him as you see them both. The hadith."
"6696","850 - Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two kinds of my nation I have not yet seen: women clothed yet naked, deviating and making deviate, upon their heads like the humps of leaning camels; they will not enter Paradise nor find its scent; and men with whips in their hands like the tails of cattle, beating people with them."
"6697","851 - Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, and Suhayl from his father from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you opens upon himself a door of begging except Allah opens upon him a door of poverty."
"6698","Musnad of al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib. 1 - Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, in the month of Rabi al-Akhir of the year three hundred and six, Musab ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri narrated to us, who said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad and Ibn Abi Hazim narrated to me, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Amir ibn Sad, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: He has tasted the flavor of faith who is pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Prophet."
"6699","2 - Musab ibn Abdullah narrated to us, who said: Ibn al-Darawardi and Ibn Abi Hazim narrated to me, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Amir ibn Sad, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the servant prostrates, seven bones prostrate with him: his face, his two hands, his two knees, and his two feet."
"6700","3 - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from al-Abbas, that he said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Your uncle Abu Talib used to protect you and do for you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is in a shallow part of the Fire, and were it not for me he would be in the lowest depth."
"6701","4 - Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith who said: Al-Abbas said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Abu Talib used to protect you and defend you; did you benefit him with anything? He said: He said: I found him in the throes of the Fire, and I brought him out to the shallow part."
"6702","5 - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith who said: Al-Abbas said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me something to ask my Lord. He said: Ask your Lord for well-being. He said: Then he waited as long as Allah willed, then said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me something to ask my Lord. He said: Ask your Lord for well-being in this world and the Hereafter."
"6703","6 - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Yazid, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from al-Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"6704","7 - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Ibn al-Had, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The religion will prevail until it crosses the seas, and the seas will be traversed in the path of Allah; then there will come after you peoples who recite the Quran, saying: We have recited the Quran, who recites better than us? Who understands better than us? Or who knows better than us? Then he turned to his companions and said: Is there any good in those? They said: No. He said: Those are from you, from this nation, and those are the fuel of the Fire."
"6705","8 - Al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Kufi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Ibn Kurayb, from his father, who said: I was leading Ibn Abbas in the lane of Abu Lahab, and he said: O Kurayb, have we reached such-and-such place? He said: You are at it now. He said: Al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib narrated to me, who said: While I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in this place, a man came strutting between his two cloaks, looking at his sides, self-conceited, when Allah caused the earth to swallow him in this spot; he keeps sinking in it until the Day of Resurrection."
"6706","9 - Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated to us, Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Muawiyah, from Muadh ibn Muhammad al-Ansari, from Ibn Suhban, from al-Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no retaliation for the skull-fracture reaching the brain, nor the deep belly wound, meaning: nor the bone-displacing wound."
"6707","10 - Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Jafar ibn Tammam, from his grandfather al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade branding on the face; al-Abbas said: I brand only on the buttocks."
"6708","11 - Musa ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Isa ibn Ibrahim Abu Amr narrated to us, Afif ibn Salim narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Muadh ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Suhban, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no retaliation for the deep belly wound, nor the bone-displacing wound, nor the skull-fracture; in them is only blood-money."
"6709","12 - Musa ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Abdullah al-Rumi narrated to us, who said: Jabir ibn Yazid ibn Rifah narrated to me, from Harun ibn Abi al-Jawza, from al-Abbas who said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) under a tree; the wind blew, and what was in it of rotten leaves fell, while what was in it of green leaves remained. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is the parable of this tree? The people said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Its parable is the parable of the believer: when he trembles from fear of Allah, his sins fall from him and his good deeds remain for him."
"6710","13 - Musa ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi al-Safar, from Ibn Shurahbil, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Abbas who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while his wives were with him; they veiled themselves from me except Maymunah. A nasal dose was pounded for him and he was administered it by force. He said: Let none remain in the house but be dosed except al-Abbas, for my oath did not reach him. Then he said: Command Abu Bakr to pray with the people. Aishah said to Hafsah: Tell him that Abu Bakr, when he stands in that station, weeps. She told him, and he said: Command Abu Bakr to pray with the people. Abu Bakr prayed, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) felt relief and came out; when Abu Bakr saw him, he stepped back, and he gestured to him with his hand, stay in your place. He came and sat beside him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited from where Abu Bakr had reached."
"6711","14 - Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Muadh ibn Muhammad al-Ansari, who said: Amr ibn Madi Karib informed me: A man of Banu Kinanah suffered a skull-fracture, and Umar ibn al-Khattab wanted to retaliate from him. Al-Abbas said to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no retaliation for a skull-fracture, nor a deep wound, nor a bone-displacing wound, so he imposed the blood-money upon him."
"6712","15 - Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, al-Khidr ibn Muhammad al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Sulayman ibn Urayb who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say to Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dream of the Muslim is a part of forty parts of prophethood. Ibn Abbas said: Of sixty. Abu Hurayrah said: You hear me say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and you say: Of sixty? 16 - Ibn Abbas said: And I say: Al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib said. Abu Uthman Amr al-Naqid said: I said, I and our companions, so it is with us, Allah willing - meaning al-Abbas - from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6713","17 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm al-Antaki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Sanani narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Kathir ibn al-Abbas who said: My father al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib narrated to me, who said: I witnessed Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when the Muslims were routed, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon a mule gifted to him by Farwah ibn Nufathah al-Judhami, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began urging it into the faces of the disbelievers while I held its bridle fearing it would hasten, and Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib held the stirrup of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Call among the companions of the acacia tree. I called at the top of my voice: O companions of the acacia tree; and criers among the Ansar: O company of Ansar; then the call was restricted to Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, who were the most steadfast unto death. They said: At your service, at your service. By Allah, I likened their turning to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only to the turning of cows to their calves. He said: They advanced and fought a fierce fight; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that, he took a handful of pebbles and threw them at the faces of the people, saying: May the faces be disfigured. He said: By Allah, I kept seeing their edge blunt and their affair retreating until Allah routed them."
"6714","18 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, Qays narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib who said: I set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Medina; he turned to it and said: Allah has cleared this peninsula of polytheism, but I fear the stars will lead them astray. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how will the stars lead them astray? He said: Rain descends, and they say: We were rained upon by such-and-such star."
"6715","19 - Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, who said: Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, from Abu Ali, from Jafar ibn Tammam, from his father, from al-Abbas who said: They used to enter upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) without using the tooth-stick, so he said: You enter upon me with yellow teeth and do not use the tooth-stick? Use the tooth-stick; were it not that I would burden my nation, I would have made the tooth-stick obligatory upon them as I made ablution obligatory upon them. Aishah said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept mentioning the tooth-stick until we feared a Quran would be revealed concerning it."
"6716","20 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, who said: Nafi informed me, who said: I heard al-Abbas say to al-Zubayr: O Abu Abdullah, here the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded you to plant the banner, meaning on the day of the conquest of Mecca."
"6717","21 - Ishaq narrated to us, Sharik ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abdullah, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib concerning His saying: And the Throne of your Lord, that Day, eight will bear it above them. He said: Eight angels in the form of wild goats."
"6718","22 - Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Yahya ibn al-Ala, from his maternal uncle Shuayb ibn Khalid, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abdullah ibn Umayrah, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib who said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Batha. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know what this is? He said: We said: The clouds. He said: And the laden clouds. We said: And the laden clouds. He said: And the lofty clouds. He said: Then we fell silent. He said: Do you know how much is between heaven and earth? We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Between them is a journey of five hundred years; between every heaven to heaven is a journey of five hundred years; the thickness of every heaven is a journey of five hundred years; the seventh heaven, between its bottom and its top is as between heaven and earth; then above that are eight wild goats, between their knees and their hooves as between heaven and earth; then above that is the Throne; and nothing of the deeds of the children of Adam is hidden from Him."
"6719","23 - Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Umar ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has purified this town of polytheism, unless the stars lead them astray."
"6720","24 - Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib who said: O Messenger of Allah, did you benefit Abu Talib? He used to protect you and grow angry for you. He said: He is in a shallow part of the Fire, and were it not for me he would be in the lowest depth."
"6721","Musnad of al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas. 1 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured forth from Arafah with Usamah ibn Zayd behind him, and poured forth from Muzdalifah with al-Fadl ibn Abbas behind him. Al-Fadl said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept saying talbiyah until he stoned the Aqabah pillar."
"6722","2 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq, Sulayman ibn Yasar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, my father was reached by Islam while an old man; if I tie him on the saddle I fear he will die, and if I do not tie him he will not stay firm; shall I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Tell me, if your father owed a debt and you repaid it, would it suffice him? He said: Yes. He said: Then perform Hajj on behalf of your father."
"6723","3 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ubaydullah and al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that al-Ghumaysa - or al-Rumaysa - came complaining of her husband to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: He does not approach her. He said: He said: She lies, O Messenger of Allah; I do, but she wants to return to her first husband. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: She is not lawful for him until she tastes his little honey."
"6724","4 - Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni Abu Ayyub narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke fast at Arafah."
"6725","5 - Sulayman al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi al-Haytham narrated to us, Uthman ibn Ata narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in two white Sahuli garments."
"6726","6 - Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Azrah, from al-Shabi, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, who said: I was behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Muzdalifah; his mount did not lift its foot in the morning until it reached Muzdalifah."
"6727","7 - Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail ibn Jafar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Harmalah narrated to us, from Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Usamah ibn Zayd, that he was behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Arafat; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached the left pass below Muzdalifah, he made his camel kneel. He said: Then he came and I poured ablution water for him and he performed ablution. I said: The prayer, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The prayer is ahead of you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode until he reached Muzdalifah and prayed; then al-Fadl rode behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the morning of Muzdalifah."
"6728","8 - Kurayb said: Abdullah ibn Abbas informed me, from al-Fadl, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept saying talbiyah until he reached the pillar."
"6729","9 - Kamil narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Abu Mabad, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas - and he was behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - who said on the evening of Arafah and the morning of Muzdalifah, when they set forth: O people, upon you is calm, while he restrained his she-camel, until when he entered Muhassir - which is part of Mina - he said: Upon you is pebbles of throwing, with which the pillar is stoned; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept saying talbiyah until he stoned the pillar."
"6730","10 - Amr ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Shubah, from Mushash, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the weak of Banu Hashim to depart from Muzdalifah by night."
"6731","Amr ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, from al-Abbas ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited al-Abbas in a desert dwelling place of ours, and a dog and a donkey of ours were grazing, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Asr with them in front of him, and they were neither driven away nor moved back."
"6732","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, who said: Ibn Abbas said: al-Fadl ibn Abbas said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I kept hearing him saying the Talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah, and when he stoned it he stopped."
"6733","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from Jafar, from his father, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept saying the Talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah, and he stoned it with seven pebbles, saying Takbir with every pebble."
"6734","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank on the Day of Arafah."
"6735","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abu Mabad, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured forth from Arafah and from Muzdalifah, with tranquility upon him, until he came to Mina, and when he descended into Muhassir he said: O people, you must take pebbles the size of pebbles thrown with the fingers, meaning the pebbles of the Jamarat, gesturing with his hand with pebbles thrown with the fingers."
"6736","Abu Bakr Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, who said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a Bedouin with a beautiful daughter of his was with him, and he kept presenting her to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hoping he would marry her. He said: So I kept turning to look at her, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept taking my head and turning it away, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept saying the Talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah."
"6737","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured forth from Arafat with Usamah riding behind him, and his she-camel swerved with him while he was standing, so he struck it before he poured forth, with his hands raised not going beyond his head, and when he poured forth he moved at a gentle pace until he came to Muzdalifah, then he poured forth from Muzdalifah with al-Fadl riding behind him, and al-Fadl said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept saying the Talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah."
"6738","Abu Bakr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood inside the Kabah and did not bow and did not prostrate."
"6739","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mushash, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the weak among Banu Hashim to hasten from Muzdalifah by night."
"6740","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from Jafar, from his father, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, who said: I was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah with seven pebbles, saying Takbir with every pebble."
"6741","Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drink on the Day of Arafah."
"6742","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas: al-Fadl ibn Abbas narrated to us, who said: A woman from Khatham came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father has been overtaken by the obligation of Hajj from Allah while he is a very old man unable to remain firm on his mount. He said: Then perform Hajj on behalf of your father. Mamar said: And Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq used to narrate that he heard Sulayman ibn Yasar say that it was a woman who asked about her mother."
"6743","Harun narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, who said: al-Layth informed me, from Abd Rabbihi ibn Said, from Imran ibn Abi Anas, from Abdullah, from Rabiah ibn al-Harith, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Prayer is two by two, and you recite the Tashahhud facing forward in every two rakahs, and you beseech humbly and submit and be still, then you raise your hands, meaning: you lift them to your Lord facing with their palms toward your face, and you say: O Lord, O Lord; whoever does not do that, it is deficient."
"6744","Musnad of Fatimah daughter of the Messenger of Allah. Jabir reported: Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed nine years in Madinah without performing Hajj, then he announced among the people to go out. When he came to Dhu al-Hulayfah he prayed at Dhu al-Hulayfah, and Asma bint Umays gave birth to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, and she sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Perform Ghusl, wrap yourself with a cloth, and enter Ihram. He said: So she did. When the chest of the Messenger of Allah's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mount settled on the back of al-Bayda, he entered Ihram and we entered Ihram with him, knowing nothing but Hajj, and for it we had set out, with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among us, and the Quran was being revealed to him and he knew its interpretation, and he only did what he was commanded. Jabir said: I looked before me and behind me and to my right and to my left as far as my sight reached, with people walking and riding, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept saying the Talbiyah, saying: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, there is no partner for You, here I am; indeed praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion; there is no partner for You. When we arrived at Makkah, he began by touching the Corner, then he ran three circuits and walked four. When he finished his Tawaf and went to the Maqam, he said: Allah said: And take the Station of Ibrahim as a place of prayer. He prayed two rakahs behind the Station of Ibrahim. Jafar ibn Muhammad said: My father said: He used to recite in them the chapters of Tawhid: Say, O disbelievers, and Say, He is Allah, One. He said: And that was not mentioned from Jabir. Jabir said: Then he went to the Corner and touched it, then he went to al-Safa and said: We begin with what Allah began with: Indeed al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah. He ascended al-Safa until the House appeared to him, and he said Takbir three times, and said: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise; He gives life and causes death; in His hand is good, and He is over all things capable, three times, and he supplicated during that. Then he descended from al-Safa and walked until his feet sloped down in the valley bottom, then he ran until his feet ascended in the valley bottom, then he walked to al-Marwah and ascended al-Marwah until the House appeared to him, and he said the same as he had said on al-Safa. He circumambulated seven times, then he said: Whoever does not have the sacrificial animal with him, let him exit Ihram, and whoever has the sacrificial animal with him, let him remain in his Ihram, for had it not been that the sacrificial animal is with me, I would have exited Ihram, and had I known beforehand what I know now, I would have entered Ihram for Umrah. He said: And Ali came from Yemen, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: With what did you enter Ihram, O Ali? He said: I said: O Allah, I enter Ihram with what Your Messenger enters Ihram with. He said: Then I have the sacrificial animal with me, so do not exit Ihram. Ali said: I entered upon Fatimah and she had applied kohl and worn dyed clothes, so I said: Who commanded you with this? She said: My father commanded me. He said: And Ali used to say in Iraq: So I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining about Fatimah and seeking confirmation about what she had said, and he said: She spoke the truth; I commanded her. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed one hundred camels of that, with his own hand sixty-three camels, and Ali sacrificed the rest, then he took a piece from every camel and they were cooked together, and they both ate of the meat and drank of the broth. Suraqah ibn Malik ibn Jushum said: O Messenger of Allah, is this for this year of ours or forever? He said: Rather forever; Umrah has entered into Hajj, and he interlaced his fingers."
"6745","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from his father, from al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Fatimah daughter of the Messenger of Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a bone with meat in her house, then Bilal came and announced the prayer to him, so he stood to pray, and I took hold of his garment and said: O father, will you not perform ablution? He said: For what should I perform ablution, my dear daughter? I said: Because of what the fire has touched. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is not the purest of your food what the fire has touched?"
"6746","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Shaybah ibn Na'amah, from Fatimah bint al-Husayn, from Fatimah al-Kubra, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the sons of every mother there is an 'asabah (paternal kin) to whom they affiliate, except the children of Fatimah, for I am their guardian and I am their 'asabah."
"6747","Al-Husayn ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Amr ibn Muhammad al-'Anqazi narrated to us, Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Yahya ibn Ja'dah, he said: Fatimah, daughter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Indeed 'Isa son of Maryam remained among the Children of Israel for forty years."
"6748","Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Saminah al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Hanafi narrated to us, Musa ibn Ya'qub al-Zam'i narrated to us, from Hashim ibn Hashim, from Abdullah ibn Wahb, from Umm Salamah, she said: Fatimah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he confided something to her and she wept, then he confided something to her and she laughed. So I asked her about it, and she said: He informed me that he would be taken (in death) in this year, so I wept. Then he said: Would it not please you to be the mistress of the women of Paradise except so-and-so? So I laughed."
"6749","Ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Saminah narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, from Firas, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Aishah, similar to it."
"6750","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Firas, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: Fatimah came walking as if her walk were the walk of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said: Welcome to my daughter, and he seated her on his right or on his left, and he confided a report to her and she wept, then he confided a report to her and she laughed. So I said: I have never seen like today grief closer to joy! What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) confide to you? She said: I would not disclose the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then when he passed away I asked her, and she said: He said: Indeed Jibril used to come to me and review the Qur'an with me once, and this year he came to me and reviewed it with me twice, and I see my term has only drawn near, and what an excellent predecessor I am for you, and you are the first of my household to join me. So I wept for that. Then he said: Are you not pleased to be the mistress of the believing women, or the women of this ummah? She said: So I laughed."
"6751","Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, al-Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated to us, he said: Rabi'ah al-Ma'afiri narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: We buried with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, and when he finished he left and stood in the middle of the road, and there was a woman approaching; we did not think he knew her. When she drew near, she was Fatimah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: O Fatimah, what brought you out of your house? She said: I came, O Messenger of Allah, to the people of this house and showed mercy toward their deceased, or consoled them; I do not remember which of the two she said. Rabi'ah said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perhaps you reached the al-kuda with them? She said: Allah forbid, and I have heard you mention concerning it what you mention. He said: Had you reached the al-kuda you would not have seen Paradise until the grandfather of your mother, or the father of your father, sees it; Abu Yahya doubted. So I asked Rabi'ah about al-kuda, and he said: I think it is the graveyards. He said: When I saw Rabi'ah doubt, I met Yazid ibn Abi Habib and informed him of Rabi'ah's hadith and asked him about al-kuda, and he said: They are the graveyards. Yazid ibn Abi Habib said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) attended the funeral of a man, and when it was placed to pray over it he saw a woman, and he asked about her, and it was said to him: She is the sister of the deceased, O Messenger of Allah. So he said to her: Go back, and he did not pray over it until she disappeared from view. Yazid said: And Umm Salamah attended Abu Salamah."
"6752","Jubarah ibn Mughallis narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Wasim al-Jammal narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Hasan informed us, from his mother Fatimah bint al-Husayn, from her father Husayn ibn Ali, from his mother Fatimah bint Muhammad, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let no man blame anyone but himself who spends the night with the smell of ghamar (grease from meat) on his hand."
"6753","Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, from Abu al-Jahhaf Dawud ibn Abi Awf, from Muhammad ibn Amr al-Hashimi, from Zaynab bint Ali, from Fatimah bint Muhammad, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at Ali and said: This one is in Paradise, and among his partisans are a people who learn Islam then reject it; they have a nickname, they are called al-Rafidah. Whoever meets them, let him kill them, for they are polytheists."
"6754","Isa ibn Salim narrated to us, Wahb ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Qurashi narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from al-Hasan ibn Ali, that he entered the place of ablution and found a morsel, or he said: a crust, in the channel of excrement and urine, so he took it and removed the filth from it and washed it well, then handed it to his servant boy and said: O boy, remind me of it when I perform ablution. When he performed ablution he said to the boy: O boy, hand me the morsel, or he said: the crust. He said: O my master, I ate it. He said: Then go, for you are free for the sake of Allah. The boy said to him: O my master, for what did you free me? He said: Because I heard from Fatimah bint Rasul Allah mentioning from her father the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever takes a morsel or crust from the channel of excrement and urine, and removes the filth from it and washes it well then eats it, it will not settle in his stomach until he is forgiven. So I would not keep in service a man from the people of Paradise."
"6755","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, he said: We came to Jabir ibn Abdullah while he was among Banu Salamah, and we asked him about the pilgrimage of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the hadith at length, and it is with us written in the Musnad of Jabir."
"6756","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Jumay', from Abu al-Tufayl, he said: Fatimah came to Abu Bakr and said: O Caliph of the Messenger of Allah, did you inherit the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or his family? He said: Rather his family. She said: Then what of the share of the Messenger of Allah? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah provides a prophet with sustenance then takes him, He makes it for the one who stands after him. So I saw fit to return it to the Muslims. She said: You and the Messenger of Allah know best."
"6757","Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, that the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered to Fatimah and said to her: Go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and say to him: Your wives adjure you to be just concerning the daughter of Abu Quhafah. So she came to him and mentioned that to him. He said: Do you not love whom I love? She said: Yes. He said: Then I love this one."
"6758","Al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abdullah ibn al-Hasan, from Fatimah bint Rasul Allah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered the mosque, would say: In the name of Allah, and peace upon the Messenger of Allah. O Allah, forgive me my sins and open for me the doors of Your mercy. And when he went out he would say: In the name of Allah, and peace upon the Messenger of Allah. O Allah, forgive me my sins and open for me the doors of Your bounty."
"6759","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from his father, that Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to him, that Aishah narrated to him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called his daughter Fatimah and confided to her and she wept, then confided to her and she laughed. Aishah said: So I said to Fatimah: What is this that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) confided to you and you wept, then confided to you and you laughed? She said: He confided to me and informed me of his death, so I wept. Then he confided to me and informed me that I am the first of his family to follow him, so I laughed."
"6760","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Fatimah asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a servant, so he said: Shall I not guide you to what is better than that? You glorify Allah, magnify Him, and praise Allah when you go to your bed one hundred times."
"6761","Al-Sami narrated to us, Sukayn ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ja'far narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: When Ali was killed, Hasan ibn Ali stood as an orator, and he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: To proceed, by Allah, you have killed tonight a man on a night in which the Qur'an was sent down, and in which 'Isa son of Maryam was raised, and in which Yusha' ibn Nun, the youth of Musa, peace be upon him, was killed."
"6762","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Sukayn narrated to us, he said: And my father narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Jabir, from his father, from al-Hasan ibn Ali, the like of this, and he added in it: And in it repentance was accepted from the Children of Israel. And he said: By Allah, no one before him surpassed him, nor did anyone after him reach him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would indeed send him on an expedition with Jibril on his right and Mika'il on his left, and by Allah he left neither yellow nor white except seven or eight hundred dirhams which he had set aside to buy a servant."
"6763","Muhammad ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Mu'ammal narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Sa'di say: I said to al-Hasan: What do you remember from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I heard him supplicate with this supplication: O Allah, guide us among those You have guided, and grant us well-being among those You have granted well-being, and take us as allies among those You have taken as allies, and bless for us what You have given, and protect us from the evil of what You have decreed. Indeed You decree and none decrees upon You, and indeed whoever You befriend is not humiliated. Blessed and exalted are You."
"6764","Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Husayn al-Ashqar narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Sawwar Abu Idris, from al-Musayyab ibn Najabah, he said: I entered upon al-Hasan ibn Ali, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: War is deceit."
"6765","Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Nafi' narrated to us, al-Ala' ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, he said: I heard al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray in your houses, do not take them as graves, and do not take my house as a festival. Send blessings upon me and greet me, for your blessings and greetings reach me wherever you are."
"6766","Musa ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, he said: I heard Abu al-Hawra' al-Sa'di say: I asked al-Hasan ibn Ali: Did you hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I found a date from the dates of charity and put it in my mouth, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it from my mouth with his saliva and threw it among the dates. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you take it? He said: Because charity is not lawful for the family of Muhammad. And he would say: Leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt, for truthfulness is tranquility and lying is doubt. He said: And he used to teach us this supplication: O Allah, guide me among those You have guided, grant me well-being among those You have granted well-being, take me as an ally among those You have taken as allies, bless for me what You have given, and suffice me the evil of what You have decreed. Indeed You decree and none decrees upon You, and indeed whoever You befriend is not humiliated. Blessed and exalted are You."
"6767","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, Sa'd ibn Tarif narrated to us, from Umayr ibn Ma'mun ibn Zurarah, from al-Hasan ibn Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The gift for the fasting person is oil and incense."
"6768","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Yahya, he said: I was between al-Husayn and al-Hasan, and Marwan was exchanging insults; al-Hasan kept restraining al-Husayn. Marwan said: A cursed household. Al-Hasan became angry and said: Did you say: A cursed household? By Allah, Allah cursed you upon the tongue of His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while you were in the loins of your father."
"6769","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Abu al-Hawra', from al-Hasan ibn Ali, he said: My grandfather the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me words to say in the qunut of witr: O Allah, grant me well-being among those You have granted well-being, take me as an ally among those You have taken as allies, guide me among those You have guided, and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed. Indeed You decree and none decrees upon You, and indeed whoever You befriend is not humiliated. Glory be to You, blessed and exalted are You."
"6770","Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Yahya al-Nakha'i, that al-Hasan and al-Husayn were passed by Marwan, and he said to them an ugly saying. Al-Hasan or al-Husayn said: By Allah, then by Allah, Allah cursed you while you were in the loins of al-Hakam upon the tongue of His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So Marwan fell silent."
"6771","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ar'arah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Huna'i narrated to us, al-Bara' ibn Abi Fadalah narrated to us, al-Hadrami informed us, from Abu Maryam, the foster-child of al-Jarud, he said: I was in Kufah, and al-Hasan ibn Ali stood as an orator and said: O people, last night I saw a wonder in my dream. I saw the Lord, exalted, above His Throne, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came until he stood at one of the legs of the Throne. Then Abu Bakr came and placed his hand on the shoulder of the Messenger of Allah, then Umar came and placed his hand on the shoulder of Abu Bakr, then Uthman came and was at a distance. He said: My Lord, ask Your servants for what they killed me? He said: Then two spouts of blood poured from the heaven to the earth. He said: It was said to Ali: Do you not see what al-Hasan narrates? He said: He narrates what he saw."
"6772","Sufyan ibn Waki' narrated to us, Jumay' ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ijli narrated to us, from Mujahid or Mujalid, from Tuhrub al-Ijli, from al-Hasan ibn Ali, he said: I will not fight after a vision I saw. I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placing his hand on the Throne, and I saw Abu Bakr placing his hand on the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I saw Umar placing his hand on Abu Bakr, and I saw Uthman placing his hand on Umar, and I saw blood beneath them. I said: What is this blood? It was said: The blood of Uthman; Allah seeks retribution for it."
"6773","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hariz ibn Uthman, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Awf, from al-Hasan ibn Ali, that he said to Abu al-A'war: Woe to you, did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not curse Ri'l and Dhakwan, and Amr ibn Sufyan?"
"6774","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from his father, from al-Hasan ibn Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the house of Fatimah, and he mentioned the hadith, and we wrote it in the ahadith of Ibn Numayr in the dictation."
"6775","Isma'il ibn Musa ibn bint al-Suddi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Khuthaym al-Hilali narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Yasar al-Hamdani, from Ali ibn Abi Talhah, freedman of Banu Umayyah, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan performed pilgrimage, and Mu'awiyah ibn Hudayj performed pilgrimage with him, and he was among the most abusive of people toward Ali. He said: He passed through Madinah, while Hasan ibn Ali and a group of his companions were sitting. It was said to him: This is Mu'awiyah ibn Hudayj, the abuser of Ali. He said: Bring the man to me. A messenger came to him and said: Answer him. He said: Who? He said: Al-Hasan ibn Ali invites you. So he came to him and greeted him. Al-Hasan said to him: Are you Mu'awiyah ibn Hudayj? He said: Yes. He repeated that to him. He said: Are you the abuser of Ali? It was as if he felt ashamed. Al-Hasan said to him: By Allah, if you come to him at the Hawd, and I do not think you will come to it, you will find him with his waist-wrapper rolled up on his leg, driving away the banners of the hypocrites as the stray camel is driven away; the word of the truthful one believed. And indeed he fails who invents."
"6776","Al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq al-Jarmi narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Humayd al-Kindi, from Sa'd al-Iskaf, from Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ali, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: Jibril came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, indeed Allah loves three of your companions, so love them: Ali ibn Abi Talib, Abu Dharr, and al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad. He said: Then Jibril came to him and said to him: O Muhammad, indeed Paradise longs for three of your companions, and with him was Anas ibn Malik, and he hoped it would be for some of the Ansar. He said: He wanted to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about them but was in awe of him. So he went out and met Abu Bakr and said: O Abu Bakr, I was just now with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Jibril came to him and said: Indeed Paradise longs for three of your companions. I hoped it would be for some of the Ansar, but I was in awe to ask him. Would you enter upon the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him? He said: I fear to ask him lest I not be among them and my people gloat over me. Then Umar ibn al-Khattab met me, and he said to him the like of what Abu Bakr said. He said: Then he met Ali, and Ali said to him: Yes, if I am among them I praise Allah, and if I am not among them I praise Allah. So he entered upon the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Anas informed me that he was just now with you, and that Jibril came to you and said: O Muhammad, indeed Paradise longs for three of your companions. He said: Who are they, O Prophet of Allah? He said: You are among them, O Ali, and Ammar ibn Yasir, and he will witness with you scenes whose merit is clear and whose good is great, and Salman, and he is from us, the Ahl al-Bayt, and he is sincere, so take him for yourself."
"6777","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I said to Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid: Did you see Husayn ibn Ali? He said: Black of head and beard except a few hairs here at the front of his beard; I do not know whether he dyed and left that place in imitation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or whether nothing except that had turned white. He said: And I saw Hasan when the prayer had been established prostrate between the imam and some people, and it was said to him: Sit, and he said: The prayer has been established."
"6778","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Amir, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Uthman, from his mother Fatimah bint al-Husayn, from her father Husayn ibn Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not keep looking at lepers, and when you speak to them let there be between you and them the length of a spear."
"6779","Ya'qub ibn Isa, neighbor of Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Muttalib, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Abdullah, from Zayd ibn Ali ibn Husayn, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed defending his right is a martyr."
"6780","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, he said: Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah al-Ansari narrated to me, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Ali ibn Husayn narrate from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The miser is he in whose presence I am mentioned and he does not send blessings upon me."
"6781","Abd al-Rahman ibn Sallam al-Jumahi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from his mother, from Fatimah bint al-Husayn, that she heard her father al-Husayn ibn Ali say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no Muslim man or woman afflicted by a calamity, even if its time is distant, who renews istirja' (saying: to Allah we belong and to Him we return) for it, except that Allah renews for him at that moment and gives him the reward He promised him for it on the day he was afflicted by it."
"6782","Hawtharah narrated to us, Hisham Abu al-Miqdam narrated to us, with his chain, similar to it."
"6783","Jubarah narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Ala' narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah al-Uqayli, from al-Husayn ibn Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed in Friday there is an hour in which no one is cupped except that he dies."
"6784","Jubarah narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Ala' narrated to us, from Marwan ibn Salim, from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, from Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has a child born to him and calls the adhan in his right ear and the iqamah in his left ear, Umm al-Sibyan (the mother of boys, i.e., evil affliction) will not harm him."
"6785","Jubarah narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Ala' narrated to us, from Marwan ibn Salim, from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, from al-Husayn ibn Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The protection of my ummah from drowning, when they ride, is to say: In the name of Allah is its course and its anchorage. Indeed my Lord is Forgiving, Merciful, and: They did not esteem Allah as He deserves, the verse."
"6786","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Salim narrated to us, Husayn ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Zayd, from his father, from al-Husayn ibn Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform ablution and wash the place of his prostration with water until he made it flow over the place of prostration."
"6787","Kamil ibn Talhah narrated to us, Abu Hisham al-Qannad narrated to us, from al-Husayn ibn Ali, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The cheated one is neither praised nor rewarded."
"6788","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mus'ab ibn Muhammad, from Ya'la ibn Abi Yahya, from Fatimah bint Husayn, from her father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The beggar has a right, even if he comes on a horse."
"6789","Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Umar ibn Shabib narrated to us, from Yusuf al-Sabbagh, from al-Husayn, and I know it only from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever witnesses a matter and dislikes it is like one who was absent from it, and whoever is absent from a matter and is pleased with it is like one who witnessed it."
"6790","Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Abu al-Hawra', he said: Al-Husayn ibn Ali said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me words to say in the qunut of witr: My Lord, guide me among those You have guided, grant me well-being among those You have granted well-being, take me as an ally among those You have taken as allies, bless for me what You have given, and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed. Indeed You decree and none decrees upon You, and indeed You do not humiliate whom You befriend. Blessed are You, our Lord, and exalted."
"6791","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma' narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Ya'qub narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, freedman of al-Hasan ibn Ali, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mounted me behind him one day, and he confided to me a report which I do not narrate to anyone among people. The most beloved cover for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to relieve himself was a target, or a dense grove of date-palms, meaning: a wall. So he entered a wall belonging to a man of the Ansar, and there was a camel in it. When it saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) it panicked and its eyes shed tears. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to it and wiped its head to its hump and its temples, so it calmed. He said: Who is the master of this camel? To whom does this camel belong? A youth of the Ansar came and said: It is mine, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do you not fear Allah concerning this beast? Allah has given you ownership of it, for it complained to me that you starve it and overwork it."
"6792","Shayban narrated to us, Mahdi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Ya'qub narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, freedman of al-Hasan ibn Ali, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mounted me behind him one day, and he confided to me a report which I do not narrate to anyone among people. He said: The most beloved cover of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a need was a target or a dense grove. Then he mentioned similar to the hadith of Abdullah ibn Muhammad."
"6793","Mus'ab ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abdullah ibn Ja'far, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing two garments dyed with saffron: a cloak and a turban."
"6794","Mus'ab narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abdullah ibn Ja'far, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people shooting arrows at a ram and disliked that, and said: Do not mutilate beasts."
"6795","Musa ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, he said: I heard Muwwarriq, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came from a journey, and I and a boy of Banu Hashim met him, and he carried us."
"6796","Musa ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Musafi' narrated to me, that Mus'ab ibn Shaybah informed him, from Uqbah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever doubts in his prayer, let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting."
"6797","Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Isma'il ibn Abi Hakim, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta."
"6798","Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Fadl, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear his ring on his right."
"6799","Al-Qasim ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Khadijah glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl."
"6800","Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, al-Harith ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Jabir, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped on his neck after he was poisoned."
"6801","Khalifah ibn Khayyat narrated to us, Bakr ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Khadijah glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl, in which there is neither noise nor fatigue."
"6802","Muhriz ibn Awn ibn Abi Awn narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating cucumber with fresh dates."
"6803","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Fadl, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, he said: I saw the ring of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on his right."
"6804","Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Saminah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Musafi', from Mus'ab ibn Shaybah, from Uqbah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you doubts in his prayer and does not know how much he prayed, let him prostrate two prostrations when he finishes his prayer."
"6805","Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Ja'far ibn Khalid, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, he said: When Ja'far was announced dead, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prepare food for the family of Ja'far, for there has come to them a matter that occupies them, or they are occupied by it."
"6806","Abu Salamah ibn al-Sabbak narrated to us, Makhlad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abdullah ibn Musafi', from Uqbah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever doubts in his prayer, let him prostrate two prostrations after he gives salam."
"6807","Isma'il ibn Sayf al-Basri narrated to us, Umar ibn Harun al-Balkhi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Ja'far, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see one who renounces the world, draw near to him, for wisdom is cast to him."
"6808","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Talhah ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Musa ibn Talhah, Aqil ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, he said: Quraysh came to Abu Talib and said: Your nephew harms us in our assembly and in our mosque, so forbid him from harming us. He said: O Aqil, bring me Muhammad. So I went and brought him. He said: O son of my brother, your cousins claim you harm them in their assembly and mosque, so refrain from that. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his sight to the heaven and said: Do you see this sun? They said: Yes. He said: I am no more able to leave that for you than for you to kindle for me a flame from it. Abu Talib said: The son of my brother has not lied to us; go back."
"6809","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from al-Furat Abu Abdullah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: I was sitting with Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Mas'ud, and Ibn al-Zubayr had appointed him over the judiciary of Kufah, when the letter of Ibn al-Zubayr came to him: Peace upon you, to proceed: You used to ask me about the grandfather, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I taken from this ummah an intimate friend besides my Lord, I would have taken Ibn Abi Quhafah, but he is my brother in religion and my companion in the cave. And he made the grandfather a father, so the worthiest we take by is the word of Abu Bakr."
"6810","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicate thus, and he pointed with the forefinger."
"6811","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he sat in the tashahhud, would say thus, and Yahya placed his right hand on his right thigh and his left on his left thigh, and pointed with the forefinger, and his sight did not go beyond his pointing."
"6812","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah, he said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far said to Ibn al-Zubayr, or Ibn al-Zubayr to Ibn Ja'far: Do you remember the day we met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I and you and Ibn Abbas, and he carried us and left you?"
"6813","Zuhayr and Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, they said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Yazid, Abd al-Aziz ibn Usayd narrated to us, he said: I heard a man say to Ibn al-Zubayr: Give us a fatwa concerning date-wine of jars? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade date-wine of jars."
"6814","Zuhayr narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to me, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr orate upon this pulpit, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer, or he said: in the prayers, would say: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner. To Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things capable. There is no power nor strength except by Allah. There is no god but Allah, and we worship none but Allah, Possessor of blessing, bounty, and good praise. There is no god but Allah, sincere to Him in religion even if the disbelievers dislike it."
"6815","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from a freedman of theirs called Abu al-Zubayr, that Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr would say the tahlil after every prayer, then say: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner. To Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things capable. There is no power nor strength except by Allah. There is no god but Allah, and we worship none but Allah. To Him belongs blessing and bounty, and to Him belongs good praise. There is no god but Allah, sincere to Him in religion even if the disbelievers dislike it. And Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr would say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say the tahlil with them after every prayer."
"6816","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Yusuf ibn al-Zubayr, freedman of the family of al-Zubayr, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: A man of Khath'am came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father embraced Islam while an old man unable to ride the camel, and pilgrimage is prescribed upon him; shall I perform pilgrimage on his behalf? He said: Are you his eldest child? He said: Yes. He said: Tell me, if your father had a debt and you paid it, would that suffice? He said: Yes. He said: Then perform pilgrimage on his behalf."
"6817","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Yusuf ibn al-Zubayr, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: Zam'ah had a slave-girl he had intercourse with, and she was suspected with another man who had intercourse with her. Zam'ah died while she was pregnant, and she bore a boy resembling the man she was suspected with. Sawdah mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: As for inheritance, it is his; but as for you, veil yourself from him, for he is not your brother."
"6818","Zuhayr narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: A man of the Ansar disputed with al-Zubayr before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the streams of al-Harrah with which they watered the date-palms. The Ansari said to al-Zubayr: Let the water flow. He refused, so he spoke to the Messenger of Allah about him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Irrigate, O Zubayr, then send to your neighbor. The Ansari became angry and said: O Messenger of Allah, because he is your aunt's son? The face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed color, then he said: O Zubayr, irrigate, and withhold the water until it returns to the embankment. Al-Zubayr said: By Allah, I think the verse was revealed concerning those: But no, by your Lord, they will not believe until they make you judge in what disputes between them, to His word: and submit fully."
"6819","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr while he orated, he said: Muhammad, peace be upon him, said: Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter."
"6820","Ishaq narrated to us, Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, that Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr informed them, he said: A party of Banu Tamim came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Bakr said: Appoint al-Qa'qa' ibn Ma'bad ibn Zurarah. Umar said: Appoint al-Aqra' ibn Habis. Abu Bakr said: You intended only to oppose me. Umar said: I did not intend to oppose you. They argued until their voices rose, and there was revealed: O you who believe, do not advance before Allah and His Messenger."
"6821","Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Abu Dhibyan, he said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr while he orated, he said: Muhammad, peace be upon him, said: Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter. He said: And beside him was Ibn Umar, and he said: Then by Allah he will not enter Paradise; Allah says: And their clothing therein is silk."
"6822","Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from a freedman of the family of al-Zubayr, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Sawdah bint Zam'ah, she said: A man entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father is a very old man unable to perform pilgrimage. He said: Tell me, if your father had a debt and you paid it on his behalf, would it be accepted from him? He said: Yes. He said: Then Allah is more deserving; so perform pilgrimage on behalf of your father. And Jarir narrated it from Ibn al-Zubayr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Ya'la said: This was narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr from Sawdah."
"6823","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until thirty liars emerge, among them Musaylamah, al-Ansi, and al-Mukhtar; and the worst tribes of the Arabs are Banu Umayyah, Banu Hanifah, and Thaqif."
"6824","Abu Ubaydah ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, Malik ibn Su'ayr narrated to us, Furat ibn al-Ahnaf narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, that he stood in a door entering the mosque, the mosque of Mina, and praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: These disbelieving slaves and sinners have set out against me. And he mentioned the hadith."
"6825","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abdullah ibn Hasan ibn Hasan, from his mother Fatimah bint Husayn, from her grandmother Fatimah bint Rasul Allah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered the mosque, would send blessings upon Muhammad, then say: O Allah, forgive me my sin and open for me the doors of Your mercy. And when he went out he would send blessings upon Muhammad, then say: O Allah, forgive me my sins and open for me the doors of Your mercy. Isma'il said: So I met Abdullah ibn Hasan and asked him about this hadith, and he said: When he entered he would say: O Allah, open for me the doors of Your mercy, and when he went out he would say: My Lord, open for me the doors of Your bounty."
"6826","Ubayd ibn Jannad narrated to us, Ata' ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from Ata', from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, he said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his illness, and at his head was a red band, or he said: yellow. He said: Son of my uncle, take this band and bind my head with it. So I bound his head with it. He said: Then he leaned upon me until we entered the mosque. He said: O people, I am only a mortal like you, and perhaps my departure from among you has drawn near. Whoever I have struck of his honor, or his hair, or his skin, or taken anything of his wealth, this is the honor of Muhammad and his hair and skin and wealth; let him stand and retaliate. Let none of you say: I fear enmity and rancor from Muhammad. Know that they are not of my nature nor of my character. He said: Then he left. When it was the next day I came to him, and he said: Son of my uncle, I do not think my standing yesterday sufficed for me. Take this band and bind my head with it. I bound his head with it. Then he leaned upon me until we entered the mosque, and he said the like of his saying yesterday, then said: The most beloved of you to us is he who retaliates. A man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, what of the day a beggar came to you and asked you, and you said: Who has something to lend us? And I lent you three dirhams. He said: O Fadl, give him. So I gave him. Then he said: Whoever is overcome by something, let him ask us and we will supplicate for him. A man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a cowardly man who sleeps much. He supplicated for him. Al-Fadl said: I saw him the bravest of us and the least of us in sleep. Then he came to the house of Aishah and said to the women the like of what he said to the men, then said: Whoever is overcome by something, let him ask us and we will supplicate for him. A woman gestured to her tongue. He supplicated for her. He said: She would sometimes say to me: O Aishah, perfect your prayer."
"6827","Al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Hiql ibn Ziyad narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Amr al-Saybani narrated to me, he said: Ibn al-Daylami narrated to me, he said: My father Fayruz narrated to me, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are of whom you know, and we have come from among whom you know. Who is our guardian? He said: Allah and His Messenger. He said: That suffices us."
"6828","Al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Shihab ibn Khirash narrated to us, from Shu'ayb ibn Ruziq al-Ta'ifi, he said: I was sitting with a man called al-Hakam ibn Hazn al-Kulafi, who had companionship with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he began to narrate to us. He said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as one of seven or one of nine. He gave us permission and we entered, and we said: O Messenger of Allah, we have come to you that you supplicate for us for good. He supplicated for us for good, ordered that we be lodged, and ordered something of dates for us; and circumstances then were meager. We stayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) days, and we witnessed Friday therein. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood leaning upon a bow, or he said: upon a staff, and praised Allah and extolled Him with good, light, blessed words, then said: O people, you will not be able to do all you are commanded, but be upright and draw near."
"6829","Al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Hiql narrated to us, from al-Muthanna, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Iyad ibn Ghanm, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever drinks wine, his prayer is not accepted for forty days; if he dies he goes to the Fire; if he repents Allah accepts from him. If he drinks it a second time, his prayer is not accepted for forty days; if he dies he goes to the Fire; if he repents Allah accepts from him. If he drinks it a third and fourth time, it is due upon Allah to give him to drink from the discharge of al-Khabal. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the discharge of al-Khabal? He said: The pus of the people of the Fire."
"6830","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Husayn, from Amir, from Urwah al-Bariqi, raising it, he said: Camels are honor for their owners, sheep are blessing, and good is tied in the forelocks of horses."
"6831","Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Aliyah and a companion of mine came to me and said: Come, for you two are younger and retain hadith better than I. So we set out until we came to Bishr ibn Asim al-Laythi. Abu al-Aliyah said: Narrate to these two a hadith. Bishr said: Uqbah ibn Malik al-Laythi narrated to us, and he was of his clan, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition which raided a people. A man of the people broke away, and a man of the expedition followed him with his sword unsheathed. A man of the people said: I am a Muslim, I am a Muslim. He did not consider it. He struck him and killed him. The report reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said concerning it a severe saying. It reached the killer. While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was orating, the killer said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah he said what he said only seeking refuge from killing. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from him and from those before him among people, and continued his oration. Then he repeated, saying: O Messenger of Allah, he said what he said only seeking refuge from killing. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from him and from those before him among people. He could not refrain from saying a third time. He turned to him with displeasure recognized on his face, and said: Indeed Allah, mighty and exalted, has refused me to kill a believer, three times."
"6832","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Nukri narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Harb ibn Surayj narrated to us, he said: A man of Bal'adawiyyah narrated to me, he said: My grandfather narrated to me, he said: I set out to Madinah and alighted at the valley, and there were two men with one goat between them, and the buyer was saying to the seller: Deal with me well. I said to myself: Is this the Hashimi who misled people he himself? I looked, and there was a man of goodly body, large forehead, fine nose, fine eyebrows, and from the pit of his throat to his navel like a black thread, black hair, and he was between two worn garments. He drew near us and said: Peace upon you. They returned it to him. Soon the buyer called, saying: O Messenger of Allah, tell him to deal well with me. He extended his hand and said: You own your wealth. I hope to meet Allah, mighty and exalted, on the Day of Resurrection with none of you seeking me for anything I wronged him in wealth, blood, or honor, except by its right. May Allah have mercy on a man easy in selling, easy in buying, easy in taking, easy in giving, easy in paying, easy in demanding. Then he went on. I said: By Allah, I shall follow this one, for his speech is good. I followed him and said: O Muhammad. He turned to me fully and said: What do you want? I said: Are you the one who misled people and destroyed them and turned them from what their fathers worshipped? He said: That is Allah. I said: To what do you call? He said: I call the servants of Allah to Allah. He said: What do you say? He said: I bear witness there is no god but Allah and I am Muhammad the Messenger of Allah, and you believe in what Allah sent down upon me, and disbelieve in al-Lat and al-Uzza, and establish prayer, and give zakah. I said: What is zakah? He said: Our rich returns to our poor. I said: Good is what you call to. There was none on earth breathing more hateful to me than him, and he did not leave until he was more beloved to me than my child, my parents, and all people. I said: I have understood. He said: Have you understood? I said: Yes. He said: You bear witness there is no god but Allah and I am Muhammad the Messenger of Allah, and believe in what was sent down upon me? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. I come to a water where many people are, and I shall call them to what you called me to, and I hope they will follow you. He said: Yes, so call them. The people of that water embraced Islam, their men and women, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped his head."
"6833","Dawud ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Shihab al-Hannat narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn Abdullah, from Malik ibn Hubayrah, that when he followed a funeral and faced its people, he divided them into three rows, then prayed over it, and he reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No three rows pray over a dead person except that it becomes due."
"6834","Amr ibn al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Talib ibn Salma ibn Asim ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: Some of my family narrated to me, that my grandfather narrated to them, that he witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his pilgrimage in his oration, saying: Indeed your wealth and blood are forbidden to you as the sanctity of this land on this day. Let it not be known of you that you return after me disbelievers striking one another's necks. Let the witness convey to the absent, for I do not know whether I shall ever meet you after today. O Allah, bear witness over them. O Allah, I have conveyed."
"6835","Amr ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Talib ibn Salma ibn Asim ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: Some of our family narrated to me, that he heard my grandfather say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that day: Indeed Allah looked at this gathering and accepted from their doers of good, and interceded their doers of good for their doers of evil, and pardoned them all."
"6836","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd al-A'la ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Iyas al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu al-Ala', from Abd al-Rahman ibn Suhar, he said: And he was of Abd al-Qays, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until lands are swallowed with tribes of Banu so-and-so. I knew that Banu so-and-so are of the Arabs, and that non-Arabs are attributed to their villages."
"6837","Surayj ibn Yunus Abu al-Harith narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Hajjaj ibn Hajjaj, from his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what removes from me the blame of fosterage? He said: A compensation: a slave or a slave-girl."
"6838","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, from Abu al-Baddah ibn Asim ibn Adi, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the shepherds to spend the night away from Mina: they stone on the day of sacrifice, and stone the morrow and after the two days of the morrow."
"6839","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Sa'id ibn al-Mu'alla, he said: I was praying in the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me and I did not answer him. I said to him: O Messenger of Allah, I was praying. He said: Did Allah not say: Respond to Allah and the Messenger? Then he said to me: Shall I not teach you a surah which is the greatest surah in the Qur'an? All praise belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds, of the seven oft-repeated and the mighty Qur'an which I was given."
"6840","Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from Jariyah ibn Qudamah, my father's uncle informed me, that he said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, teach me something by which Allah benefits me, and make it brief that I may retain what you say. He said to him: Do not become angry. He repeated it to him many times, saying: Do not become angry."
"6841","Nafi' ibn Khalid al-Tahi narrated to us, Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, Khalid ibn Qays narrated to us, from Qatadah, from a man of Khath'am, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was among a group of his companions. I said: Are you the one who claims you are the Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes. I said: O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are most beloved to Allah? He said: Faith in Allah. I said: O Messenger of Allah, then what? He said: Then maintaining kinship. I said: O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are most hateful to Allah? He said: Associating partners with Allah. I said: O Messenger of Allah, then what? He said: Then severing kinship. I said: O Messenger of Allah, then what? He said: Then commanding wrong and forbidding right."
"6842","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Abza narrated to us, he said: My mother narrated to me, from her father, that he witnessed the spoils of Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his name was Ghurab, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named him Muslim."
"6843","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, that he heard his uncle Qutbah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in the dawn prayer: And tall date-palms with arranged clusters."
"6844","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Jushami narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, Abu al-Minhal narrated to us, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, he said: There was among us a man of the Ash'aris who had accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and witnessed with him his good, beautiful scenes, Malik, or Ibn Malik, Awf doubted. He came to us one day and said: I have come to teach you and pray with you as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray with us. He called for a great bowl and put water in it, then called for a small vessel and poured from the small vessel upon our hands, then said: Now perfect ablution. The people performed ablution, then he stood and prayed with us a complete, brief prayer. When he finished he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: I know that there are peoples who are neither prophets nor martyrs, whom prophets and martyrs envy for their place with Allah. A Bedouin man from the side of the people said, and it used to please us when we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that a Bedouin be among us, for they dare to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we do not dare. He said: O Messenger of Allah, name them for us? We saw the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brighten. He said: They are people of various tribes who love one another for Allah. By Allah, their faces are light, and they are upon light. They do not fear when people fear, nor grieve when people grieve."
"6845","Uthman narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from a shaykh called Tariq, from Amr ibn Malik al-Awsi, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, be pleased with me. He turned away from me three times. I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, indeed the Lord is to be sought for pleasure. So he was pleased with me."
"6846","Abu Sa'id al-Qawariri narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Duba'i narrated to us, Abu al-Tayyah narrated to us, he said: A man asked Abd al-Rahman ibn Hubshi, and he was a very old shaykh, saying: O Ibn Hubshi, what did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do when the devils sought to deceive him? He said: The devils descended from valleys and mountain passes intending the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); among them was a devil with a flame of fire intending to burn the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with it. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw them he was frightened. Jibril came to him and said: O Muhammad, say. He said: What shall I say? He said: Say: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah which no righteous nor wicked transcends, from the evil of what descends from heaven, and the evil of what ascends therein, and the evil of what is on earth, and the evil of what comes out of it, and the evil of night and day, and the evil of every nocturnal visitor except a visitor who comes with good, O Merciful. The fire of the devil was extinguished, and Allah, mighty and exalted, routed them."
"6847","Amr ibn al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Azrah ibn Thabit narrated to us, Ilba' ibn Ahmar al-Yashkuri narrated to us, Abu Zayd narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in dawn prayer, then ascended the pulpit and orated until noon came, then descended and prayed, then ascended the pulpit and orated to us until afternoon came, then descended and prayed, then ascended the pulpit and orated to us until the sun set. He informed us of what was and what will be. The most knowledgeable of us are the most retentive of us."
"6848","Amr ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Azrah ibn Thabit narrated to us, Ilba' ibn Ahmar narrated to us, Abu Zayd narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Draw near to me and wipe my back. I uncovered his back and wiped his back. He said: And I placed the seal between my fingers and pressed it. It was said: What is the seal? He said: Hair gathered upon his shoulder."
"6849","Amr ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Azrah ibn Thabit narrated to us, Ilba' ibn Ahmar narrated to us, from Abu Zayd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped his face and supplicated for him for beauty."
"6850","Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from al-Ashajj Ashajj Abd al-Qays, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: In you are two traits Allah loves. I said: What are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Forbearance and modesty, or forbearance and deliberation. I said: Were they in me of old or recent? He said: Rather of old. I said: Praise belongs to Allah who fashioned me upon two traits He loves."
"6851","Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Hassan al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Al-Muthanna al-Abdi Abu Munazil, one of Banu Ghanm, narrated to us, from al-Ashajj al-Asari, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a company of Abd al-Qays to visit him. They came, and when they arrived the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose for them. They made their camels kneel and the people hastened to him, wearing only their travel clothes. Al-Asari stayed tying the camels of his companions and his own camel, then took out his clothes from his bag, and that was before the eyes of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In you are two traits Allah and His Messenger love. He said: What are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Deliberation and forbearance. He said: Something I was fashioned upon or something I affect? He said: No, rather you were fashioned upon it. He said: Praise belongs to Allah. He said: O company of Abd al-Qays, why do I see your faces changed? They said: O Prophet of Allah, we are in an unhealthy land, and we used to take of these drinks what cuts the flesh in our bellies. When we were forbidden vessels, that is what you see in our faces. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Vessels neither permit nor forbid, but every intoxicant is forbidden. It is not that you sit and drink until, when the veins are drunk, you boast, and a man leaps upon his cousin and strikes him with the sword, leaving him lame. He said: And on that day among the people was the lame one whom that had struck."
"6852","Muhammad ibn Sudran Abu Ja'far narrated to us, Talib ibn Hujayr al-Abdi narrated to us, Hud al-Asari narrated to us, from his grandfather, he said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was speaking to his companions, he said: There shall come upon you from this direction a party of the best people of the East. Umar ibn al-Khattab stood and headed in that direction and met thirteen riders. He welcomed and honored them, and said: Who are the people? They said: People of Abd al-Qays. He said: What brought you to this land? Trade? They said: No. He said: Will you sell these swords of yours? They said: No. He said: Perhaps you have come seeking this man? They said: Yes. He walked with them conversing until he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said to them: This is your companion whom you seek. The people threw themselves from their mounts; some ran swiftly, some trotted, some walked, until they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and took his hand kissing it, and sat with him. Al-Ashajj remained, the youngest of the people; he made the camels kneel and tied them, gathered the baggage of the people, then came walking deliberately until he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and took his hand and kissed it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In you are two traits Allah and His Messenger love. He said: What are they, O Prophet of Allah? He said: Deliberation and composure. He said: A nature I was fashioned upon or affectation from me? He said: Rather a nature. He said: Praise belongs to Allah who fashioned me upon what Allah and His Messenger love. The people turned to some dates of theirs eating them, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began naming for them: this is such, and this is such. They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, we know their names no better than you. He said: Yes. They said to a man among them: Feed us from the remainder in your bag. He stood and brought al-Burni. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is al-Burni; it is of the best of your dates. It is a remedy, and there is no disease in it."
"6853","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from al-Ash'ath ibn Umayr al-Abdi, from his father, he said: The delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When they wanted to leave, they said: You have retained from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) all you heard from him, so ask him about date-wine. They came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in an unhealthy land in which nothing suits us but drink. He said: What is your drink? They said: Date-wine. He said: In what do you drink it? They said: In the naqir (hollowed trunk). He said: Do not drink in the naqir. They went out from him saying: By Allah, our people will not reconcile with us upon this. They returned and asked, and he said to them the like of that: Do not drink in the naqir, lest a man among you strike his cousin a blow from which he remains lame till the Day of Resurrection. They laughed. He said: What do you laugh at? They said: O Messenger of Allah, by Him who sent you with truth, we drank in a naqir of ours, and one of us rose against another and struck him a blow from which he is lame till the Day of Resurrection."
"6854","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam al-Nakha'i narrated to me, Abu Sabrah al-Nakha'i narrated to us, from Farwah ibn Musayk al-Ghutayfi, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not fight with those who come forward of my people... and he mentioned the hadith."
"6855","Hudbah ibn Khalid and Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, and his copy is from the hadith of Ibrahim, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Dahhak ibn Abi Jubayrah, he said: They had nicknames in the Jahiliyyah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called a man by his nickname, and it was said: O Messenger of Allah, he dislikes it. So Allah revealed: And do not insult one another by nicknames, to the end of the verse."
"6856","Abu Talib Abd al-Jabbar ibn Asim narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Thabit ibn al-Ajlan al-Ansari, that Abu Kathir al-Muharibi narrated to him, that Kharashah narrated to him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be after me tribulations; the sleeper therein is better than the awake, the sitter therein is better than the stander, and the stander therein is better than the walker. Whoever it comes upon, let him take his sword then go to a rock and strike it with it until it breaks, then lie down for it until it passes as it passes."
"6857","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Nu'aym ibn Hammar, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man came to him and said: Which martyrs are best? He said: Those who meet in the rank and do not turn their faces until they are killed. Those roll in the upper chambers of Paradise; your Lord laughs to them, and when He laughs in a place there is no reckoning upon him."
"6858","Abu Talib Abd al-Jabbar ibn Asim narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Makhul, from Ghudayf ibn al-Harith, from Atiyyah ibn Busr al-Mazini, he said: Ukkaf ibn Wada'ah al-Hilali came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Ukkaf, do you have a wife? He said: No. He said: Nor a slave-girl? He said: No. He said: And you are healthy and wealthy? He said: Yes, and praise belongs to Allah. He said: Then you are of the brothers of devils: either you are of the monks of Christians and you are of them, or you are of us so do as we do. Of our sunnah is marriage. Your worst are your unmarried, and the vilest of your dead are your unmarried. Your unmarried are fathers of devils whom they train; they have in myself no weapon more effective against the righteous of men and women except the married. Those are the purified, cleared of indecency. Woe to you, O Ukkaf! They are the companions of Dawud, the companions of Ayyub, the companions of Yusuf, and the companions of Kursuf. He said: What is al-Kursuf, O Messenger of Allah? He said: A man among the Children of Israel, on a coast of the sea, fasting the day and standing the night, never ceasing prayer nor fasting, then disbelieved afterward in Allah the Mighty for the sake of a woman he loved. He abandoned what he was upon of worship of his Lord, then Allah reached him by what preceded from him and turned to him. Woe to you, O Ukkaf, marry, for you are of the wavering. Ukkaf said: O Messenger of Allah, I shall not leave until you marry me to whom you wish. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have married you in the name of Allah and blessing to Karimah bint Kulthum al-Himyari."
"6859","Kamil ibn Talhah al-Jahdari narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Hudayj ibn Abi Amr, he said: I heard al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): For every nation is a term, and the term of my nation is one hundred years. When one hundred years pass over my nation, there comes to it what Allah, mighty and exalted, promised it."
"6860","Amr ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Musa said: Waqqas ibn Rabi'ah narrated to us, that al-Mustawrid narrated to them, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats a meal through a man, Allah will feed him the like of it from Hell. If he is clothed through a man with a garment, Allah will clothe him the like of it from Hell. Whoever stands through a man a stand of repute, Allah will make him stand a stand of repute and show on the Day of Resurrection."
"6861","Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad and al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, and I copied it from the hadith of Abd al-A'la, they said: Wuhayb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah narrated to us, he said: A man of them called Adi narrated to me, between him and two women was neighboring; he threw a stone at one of them and killed her. He rode to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at Tabuk, and asked him about the affair of the killed woman. He said: You pay her blood-money and do not inherit her. Adi said: It is as if I look at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon a red, young camel, saying: O people, hands are only three: the hand of Allah is the highest, the hand of the giver is middle, and the hand of the receiver is lowest. So refrain, even by bundles of firewood. Then he raised his hands and said: O Allah, I have conveyed."
"6862","Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Amr ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Zayd, from Ma'qil ibn Abi Ma'qil al-Asadi, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, Umm Ma'qil grieved when she missed pilgrimage with you. He said: Let her perform umrah in Ramadan, for an umrah in Ramadan is like a pilgrimage."
"6863","Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Mubashshir narrated to us, from Artah, he said: I heard Damrah ibn Habib say: I heard Salamah ibn Nufayl al-Sakuni say: While we were sitting with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man of people came and said: O Prophet of Allah, were you brought food from heaven? He said: I was brought food in a heated vessel. He said: Was there surplus from you in it? He said: Yes. He said: What was done with it? He said: It was raised to heaven, and it is revealed to me that I shall not remain among you but a little, and you shall not remain after me but a little. Then you shall come in scattered groups, and some of you shall annihilate others. Before the Hour is severe mortality, and after it years of earthquakes."
"6864","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from al-Nu'man ibn Salim, from Aws, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and consulted him, or confided to him, while I listened. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go to them and say to them: Kill him. Then he called him and he returned to him after he had gone. He said to him: Perhaps he says: There is no god but Allah? He said: Yes, by Allah. He said: Say to them: Release him, for it was revealed to me to fight people; when they say: There is no god but Allah, their blood is forbidden to me except by right, and their reckoning is upon Allah."
"6865","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Asim ibn Hilal informed us, from Ghadarah ibn Urwah al-Fuqaymi, he said: My father informed me, he said: I came to Madinah and entered the mosque, and people awaited prayer. A man came out to us with his head dripping from ablution he performed, or a bath he bathed. He led us in prayer. When we prayed, people stood to him saying: O Messenger of Allah, what of such? What of such? repeating it many times. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, the religion of Allah is in ease. O people, the religion of Allah is in ease."
"6866","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Amir al-Sha'bi, from Amir ibn Shahr, he said: Hamdan had fortified themselves in a mountain called al-Haql from the Abyssinians; Allah protected them by it until the Persians came to Hamdan. They remained fighting until war wearied the people and the matter lengthened upon them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) emerged. Hamdan said to me: O Amir ibn Shahr, you have been a companion of kings since you were, will you come to this man and scout for us? If you approve something for us we shall do it, and if you dislike something we shall dislike it? I said: Yes, until I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah. I sat with him, and a group came and said: O Messenger of Allah, counsel us. He said: I counsel you to fear Allah, and to hear the word of Quraysh and leave their deed. I sufficed with that, by Allah, of asking him, and I approved his affair. Then it occurred to me to return to my people until I pass by al-Najashi, and he was a friend of mine. I passed by him, and while I sat with him his young son passed, and he made him recite a tablet with him. The boy read it, and I laughed. Al-Najashi said: What do you laugh at? By Allah, thus it was sent down upon the tongue of Isa son of Maryam: The curse descends upon earth when its rulers are youths. I said: From what this boy read? He said: I returned having heard this from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and this from al-Najashi. My people embraced Islam and descended to the plain. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote this letter to Umayr Dhi Marran. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Malik ibn Mirarah al-Rahawi to all Yemen. Akk Dhu Khaywan embraced Islam. It was said to Akk: Go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and take from him protection for your people and wealth. He had a village with slaves and wealth. He came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, Malik ibn Mirarah al-Rahawi came to us calling us to Islam and we embraced Islam. I have land with slaves and wealth, so write for me a letter. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote for him: In the name of Allah, the Merciful, the Compassionate, from Muhammad the Messenger of Allah to Akk Dhu Khaywan: if he is truthful in his land, slaves, and wealth, he has protection and the covenant of Allah and the covenant of Muhammad the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Khalid ibn Sa'id wrote it."
"6867","Kamil ibn Talhah al-Jahdari narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, that Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah narrated to him, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Uqbah ibn Rafi', that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: When Allah loves a servant He protects him from the world as one of you protects his sick from water that he may heal."
"6868","Salih ibn Hatim ibn Wardan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq al-Uqayli, he said: I sat with a group, I being their fourth, and a man narrated, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There shall enter Paradise through the intercession of a man of my nation more than Banu Tamim. We said: Other than you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Other than me. I asked about him after he stood, and it was said: This is Ibn Abi al-Jad'a'."
"6869","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, he said: Damrah ibn Habib narrated to me, he said: Zughb ibn Fulan al-Azdi narrated to me, he said: Abdullah ibn Hawalah al-Azdi alighted upon us. I said to him: It reached me that two hundred were assigned to you each year and you did not accept. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us around Madinah to take spoils. We returned having taken nothing, and he recognized hardship in us. He said: O Allah, do not entrust them to me lest I be weak for them, nor entrust them to themselves lest they be unable for it, nor entrust them to people lest they prefer themselves over them."
"6870","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Salamah narrated to us, that Muslim, freedman of Khalid ibn Urfutah, narrated to him, that Khalid ibn Urfutah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"6871","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Imran ibn Zibyan, from Adi ibn Thabit, he said: A man smashed the mouth of a man in the time of Mu'awiyah, and he was given his blood-money but refused to accept until he was given threefold. A man said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever gives charity of blood or less, it is expiation for him from the day he was born till the day he gave charity."
"6872","Abu al-Rabi' Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Baghdadi, not al-Zahrani, narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Maryam, from al-Haytham ibn Malik al-Ta'i, from Abd al-Rahman ibn A'idh al-Azdi, from Abu al-Hajjaj al-Thumali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The grave says to the dead when he is placed in it: Woe to you, O son of Adam, what deceived you of me? Did you not know I am the house of trial and the house of darkness? What deceived you when you passed by me strutting? If he was righteous, a respondent answers on his behalf to the grave: What if he commanded right and forbade wrong? The grave says: Then I return upon him green, his body returns light, and his soul ascends to the Lord of the worlds. Ibn A'idh said to him: O Abu al-Hajjaj, what is al-faddad? He said: One who puts forward a foot and delays another, like your walk, O son of my brother, sometimes. He said: And on that day he dresses and adorns himself."
"6873","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar Yusuf ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Taysalah narrated to me, Ma'n ibn Tha'labah al-Mazini narrated to me, and the tribe still remained, he said: Al-A'sha al-Mazini narrated to me, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and recited to him poetry. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began repeating it, saying: ."
"6874","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Humaydah ibn al-Shamardal, from Qays ibn al-Harith, he said: I embraced Islam while I had eight wives. I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him that. He said: Choose four of them."
"6875","Abu Abdullah Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Buhlul narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: The delegation of Banu Tamim came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), among them Qays ibn al-Harith."
"6876","Abu Abdullah said: And I was told from al-Thawri, from Muhammad ibn al-Sa'ib, from Humaydah ibn al-Shamardal, from Qays ibn al-Harith, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"6877","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Kathir ibn Kathir ibn al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wada'ah, from his father, from his father al-Muttalib, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he finished his seven circuits, come until he aligns between him and the portico, and pray two rak'ahs at the edge of the circumambulation area, with none between him and the circumambulation."
"6878","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abi Farwah, that Abu Hazim, freedman of Abu Ruhm al-Ghifari, informed him, from Abu Ruhm and another, that they were two horsemen on the day of Hunayn and were given six shares: four for their two horses and two for themselves. They sold the two shares for two young camels."
"6879","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Hatim narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Amr ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri narrated to us, he said: Al-Zibriqan ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Umayyah narrated to me, from his father, from Amr ibn Umayyah, he said: Uthman ibn Affan, or Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, passed by a cloak and deemed it costly. It was passed with to Amr ibn Umayyah, and he bought it and clothed his wife Sukhaylah bint Ubaydah ibn al-Harith ibn al-Muttalib with it. Uthman, or Abd al-Rahman, passed by him and said: What did the cloak you bought do? Amr said: I gave it in charity to Sukhaylah bint Ubaydah. He said: Whatever you do for your family is charity. Amr said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that. What Amr said was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Amr spoke truthfully. All you do for your family is charity upon them."
"6880","Zahmawayh narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Ibn Shihab said: Ja'far ibn Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri narrated to us, from his father, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating from a shoulder, biting from it, then coming to prayer and praying without performing ablution."
"6881","Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Dawud ibn Amr ibn Zuhayr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah al-Darir narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Urwah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon us while with us was a boy complaining. He said: What is this? They said: We suspect the evil eye in him. He said: Why do you not seek ruqyah for him from the eye?"
"6882","Surayj ibn Yunus Abu al-Harith narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I am only a mortal, and you dispute to me. Perhaps one of you is more eloquent in his plea than another, so I judge according to what I hear from him. Whoever I judge for him something of his brother's right, let him not take anything of it, for I only cut for him a piece of the Fire."
"6883","Ghassan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Urwah, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You dispute to me, and I am only a mortal. Perhaps some of you are more eloquent in plea than others. Whoever I judge for him of his brother's right, let him not take it, for I only cut for him a piece of the Fire."
"6884","Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah informed me, from Nafi', he said: Zayd ibn Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He who drinks in a vessel of silver only gurgles in his belly the fire of Hell."
"6885","Dawud ibn Amr narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from his father, from al-Minhal, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father."
"6886","And from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: Are you not pleased to be to me as Harun was to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me?"
"6887","Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abu Qilabah, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from her mother Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray upon the khumrah (small mat)."
"6888","Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Saminah al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Hanafi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, from Uthman al-Akhnasi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'd ibn Yarbu', from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us in the Farewell Pilgrimage: It is only this pilgrimage, then sitting upon the backs of mats in houses. Ibn Abi Saminah said: It is only Sa'id, but thus he said."
"6889","Muhammad ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Hanafi narrated to us, Musa ibn Ya'qub al-Zam'i narrated to us, from Hashim ibn Hashim, from Abdullah ibn Wahb, from Umm Salamah: Fatimah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he confided something to her and she wept, then confided something to her and she laughed. I asked her about it, and she said: He informed me that he would be taken in this year, so I wept. Then he said to me: Would it not please you to be the mistress of the women of Paradise? So I laughed."
"6890","Muhammad ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, from Firas, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Aishah, similar to it."
"6891","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Samina narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Fudayl, from Atiyya, from Abu Said, from Umm Salama, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) covered Ali, Fatima, Hasan and Husayn with a cloak, then said: These are my Ahl al-Bayt, to You, not to the Fire. Umm Salama said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, am I among them? He said: No, and you are upon good."
"6892","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Hunayda ibn Khalid al-Khuzai, from his mother, she said: I entered upon Umm Salama and asked her about fasting, so she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command fasting three days of every month from its beginning: Monday and Thursday, and a day I do not remember."
"6893","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: Nafi narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Umm Salama, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how about women? He said: They let down a span. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, then it will be uncovered from them. He said: Then a cubit, they do not exceed it."
"6894","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Safiyya bint Abi Ubayd, from Umm Salama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he said about trailing the hem what he said, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, then how about us? So he said: Drag it a span. She said: Then the feet will be exposed? He said: Then drag it a cubit."
"6895","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, that Umm Salama narrated to them, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) measured a span for Fatima from her waist-wrapper."
"6896","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Umm Salama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: My Lord, forgive me, have mercy on me, and guide me to the straightest path."
"6897","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated to us, Juwayriya narrated to us, from Nafi, that Sulayman ibn Yasar informed him, that a man informed him, from Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a woman suffered prolonged bleeding of blood in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so Umm Salama sought a fatwa for her from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let her consider the number of days she used to menstruate before what befell her, and their measure of the months, so she leaves prayer that amount, then when that passes and prayer comes, let her perform ghusl, wrap herself with a cloth, and pray."
"6898","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Zaynab bint Umm Salama, she said: Umm Sulaym entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Allah is not shy of the truth, is ghusl due upon a woman when she has a wet dream? He said: Yes, when she sees water. Umm Salama said: And does a woman have a wet dream? So he said: May your right hand be soiled, then whence does her child resemble her?"
"6899","Husayn ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Hafsa bint Abi Kathir, from her father Abi Kathir, he said: Umm Salama taught me, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me, he said: Say, O Umm Salama, at the Maghrib adhan: O Allah, at the approach of Your night, the retreat of Your day, the voices of Your callers, and the presence of Your prayers, I ask You to forgive me."
"6900","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Azdi narrated to us, Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, Usama ibn Zayd al-Laythi narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Rafi, freedman of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, she said: Two men came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disputing about inheritances and matters that had become effaced, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I only judge between you by my opinion so long as nothing is revealed to me, so whomever I judge for with a plea that I see, and he thereby cuts off a piece unjustly, he only cuts off thereby a piece of the Fire, a brand he will bring on his neck on the Day of Resurrection. She said: The two men wept, and each one of them said: O Messenger of Allah, this right of mine that I seek is for my companion. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, but go, aim for what is right, then draw lots, then let each one of you absolve his companion."
"6901","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah, from al-Hurr ibn al-Sayyah, from Hunayda al-Khuzai, from his wife, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Fast three days of every month from its beginning: Monday and Thursday, and the Thursday that follows it."
"6902","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Hafs ibn Ghiyath, from Hisham, from his father, from Zaynab bint Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded charity, so the wife of Abd Allah said: O Messenger of Allah, does it suffice as charity that I give charity to my husband while he is poor, and to orphaned sons of a brother of mine, though she spends like this and like this, and in every case? He said: Yes, and she was skilled with her hands."
"6903","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Sulayman ibn Suhaym narrated to me, from Umm Hakim bint Umayya, from Umm Salama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever enters ihram for Umra from Bayt al-Maqdis, he is forgiven."
"6904","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Abd Allah, from Ibn Judan, from one who narrated to him, or from his grandmother, from Umm Salama, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a maidservant of his and she delayed, so he said: Were it not for fear of retribution I would have hurt you with this whip."
"6905","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Abd Allah, from Ibn Judan, from his grandmother, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no alliance in Islam, and whatever alliance there was in Jahiliyya, it only increased in Islam in strictness."
"6906","Abu Hisham al-Rifai narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Abu Nasr Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Musawir al-Himyari, from his mother, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman who dies while her husband is pleased with her enters Paradise."
"6907","Abu Hisham narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Abu Nasr narrated to us, from Musawir, from his mother, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: No hypocrite loves you, and no believer hates you."
"6908","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, he said: Aisha and Umm Salama were asked: Which deed was most beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They both said: That which its doer persists in."
"6909","Al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Kufi al-Warraq narrated to us, Waki ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Abd Allah, from Ibn Judan, meaning from his grandmother, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one consulted is trusted."
"6910","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Ibn Umar ibn Abi Salama, from his father, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a calamity befalls one of you let him say: Indeed we belong to Allah and indeed to Him we return, O Allah with You I seek reward for my calamity, so reward me in it and replace us with better than it. When Abu Salama died, she said: I said: Indeed we belong to Allah and indeed to Him we return, O Allah with You I seek reward for my calamity, so reward me in it, and when I wanted to say: And replace me with better than it, I would say: And who is better than Abu Salama? She said: I kept on until I said it, and when her waiting period ended Abu Bakr proposed to her and she rejected him, and Umar proposed to her and she rejected him, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to her proposing to her, so she said: Welcome to the Messenger of Allah and to his messenger; convey to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and inform him that I am a jealous woman, and that I have young children, and that none of my guardians is present. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: As for your saying: I am jealous, I shall supplicate to Allah the Mighty and Majestic and He will remove your jealousy, and as for your saying: I have young children, Allah the Mighty and Majestic will suffice you for your children, and as for your guardians, there is none of them present or absent except he will approve of me. So she said to her son: Stand, O Umar, and marry the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to me, so he married her to him. And he said to her: I shall not give you less than what I gave your sister so-and-so: two jars, two water-skins, and a leather pillow stuffed with fiber. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to her while she was nursing Zaynab, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came she would take her and put her in her lap. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shy and generous, so Ammar ibn Yasir noticed her, and he was her foster brother. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to come to her one day, so Ammar came and entered upon her, and snatched Zaynab from her lap, and said: Leave this hateful wretched one by whom you have harmed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and entered, and kept turning his gaze in the house, saying: Where is Zunab? What happened to Zunab? Why do I not see Zunab? She said: Ammar came and took her away. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) consummated with his wife, and said to her: If you wish I shall stay seven for you as I stayed seven for the women."
"6911","Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, from Thabit, he said: Ibn Umm Salama narrated to me, that Abu Salama came to Umm Salama and said: I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more beloved to me than such-and-such, and I do not know what he equated it with; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No calamity befalls anyone and he says Inna lillahi wa inna ilayhi rajiun at that, then says: O Allah with You I seek reward for this calamity of mine, O Allah replace for me better than it, except Allah the Mighty and Majestic gives him. Umm Salama said: When Abu Salama was afflicted, I said: O Allah with You I seek reward for this calamity of mine, and my soul was not content to say: O Allah replace for me better than it. I said: Who is better than Abu Salama? Is he not, and is he not? Then she said that, and when her waiting period ended the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to her proposing to her, so she said: Welcome to the Messenger of Allah, there are three traits in me: I am a woman with young children, I am a woman of intense jealousy, and I am a woman with none of my guardians here present to marry me. Umar became angry for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more intensely than he had become angry for himself when she rejected him, so Umar came to her and said: Are you the one who rejects the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with what you reject him? She said: O son of al-Khattab, in me is such-and-such. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to her and said: As for what you mentioned of your jealousy, I shall supplicate to Allah to remove it, and as for what you mentioned of your children, Allah will suffice them, and as for what you mentioned that none of your guardians is present, none of your guardians present or absent dislikes me. So she said to her son: Marry the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to me, so he married him. He said: I have not diminished for you from what I gave so-and-so. Thabit said to Ibn Umm Salama: And what did he give so-and-so? He said: Two jars in which she puts her needs, a millstone, and a leather pillow stuffed with fiber. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to her; when she saw him she put Zaynab, her youngest child, in her lap. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, and when he saw her he left, and he was shy and generous. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to her; when she saw him she put her in her lap, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to her, and she put her in her lap. Then Ammar came hurrying ahead of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and snatched her from her lap, and said: Give this wretched one who prevented the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) his need. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and did not see her. He said: Where is Zunab? She said: Ammar took her. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon his wife, and she was among the women as if she were not of them, not feeling the jealousy they feel."
"6912","Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Rasi narrated to us, Abu Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Hind bint al-Harith informed me, from Umm Salama, she said: Women used to pray in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave salam they would leave, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained and whoever prayed with him as long as Allah willed, then he would stand."
"6913","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Amr ibn Muslim, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever the crescent of Dhu al-Hijja appears to him and he has a sacrifice he wants to slaughter, let him withhold from his hair and his nails."
"6914","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book, from Shuba, from Malik ibn Anas, from Amr ibn Muslim, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"6915","Hawthara ibn Ashras Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Uqba informed me, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Fatima: Bring me your husband and your two sons. So she brought them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast over them a Khaybari cloak of mine that had been under me, which we had taken from Khaybar, then said: O Allah, these are the family of Muhammad, peace be upon him, so place Your prayers and blessings upon the family of Muhammad as You placed them upon the family of Ibrahim; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. Umm Salama said: So I lifted the cloak to enter with them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pulled it from my hand and said: You are upon good."
"6916","Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, Nafi narrated to us, he said: Umm Salama said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever drinks in a vessel of silver, he only gurgles in his belly the fire of Hell."
"6917","Shayban narrated to us, Jarir said: I asked Abd al-Rahman al-Sarraj, so I said: Do you know from whom he narrates it? He said: Yes, he narrated it from Zayd ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr al-Siddiq, he said: And Umm Salama was the maternal aunt of Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman."
"6918","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Samina narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Uthman, he said: Umm Salama said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was speaking to a man, and when he stood he said: O Umm Salama, who is this? I said: Dihya al-Kalbi, and I did not know he was Jibril, peace be upon him, until I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrating to his Companions what had been between us. He said: I said to Abu Uthman, who narrated this to you? He said: Usama ibn Zayd narrated to me."
"6919","Shayban narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Huddani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Umm Salama used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hajj is the jihad of every weak one."
"6920","Ubayd Allah ibn Muadh ibn Muadh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr al-Laythi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Muslim ibn Ammar ibn Ukayma, he said: I heard Said ibn al-Musayyab say: I heard Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has a sacrifice to slaughter, when the crescent of Dhu al-Hijja appears, let him not take from his hair nor from his nails until he sacrifices."
"6921","Abu al-Rabi Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Zaynab bint Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a slave girl who was in the house of Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he saw yellowness on her face, so he said: She has been afflicted by the evil eye, so perform ruqya for her."
"6922","Sulayman ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Abu Kab, meaning the silk merchant, narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salama, she said: Among the most frequent supplications of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he was in my house was: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, why is this among your most frequent supplications? He said: There is no heart except it is between two fingers of the fingers of the Lord; what He wills He keeps upright, and what He wills He causes to deviate."
"6923","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to read: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Merciful, All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds, meaning letter by letter."
"6924","Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Ismail, meaning Ibn Ayyash, narrated to us, Ismail ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Water is poured over the urine of a boy, and the urine of a girl is washed."
"6925","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Nabhan, from Umm Salama, she said: I and Maymuna were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then Ibn Umm Maktum came seeking permission, and that was after the hijab had been imposed. He said: Stand up. They both said: He is blind, he does not see us. He said: Are you two blind, do you not see him?"
"6926","Hawthara narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadala narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The urine of a boy, water is poured over it pouring so long as he has not eaten food, and the urine of a girl is washed washing whether she has eaten or not."
"6927","Khalid ibn Mirdas narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Kathir, from Abu Abd Allah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is tried with judging between Muslims, let him not judge while angry, let him equalize between them in looking, sitting, and gesturing, and let him not raise his voice over one of the two disputants above the other."
"6928","Abu Mamar al-Hudhali narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umara narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from an umm walad of Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, she said: I used to lengthen my hem, passing by filthy places and clean places, so I entered upon Umm Salama and asked her about that, so she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: What comes after it purifies it."
"6929","Harun ibn Abd Allah al-Hammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Suqa, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, he heard Umm Salama say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the army that will be swallowed up, Umm Salama said: So I said: Perhaps among them is one compelled? He said: They will be resurrected according to their intentions."
"6930","Harun narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yuhannis narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Sufyan ibn Said al-Akhnasi narrated to me, from his grandmother Hukayma, from Umm Salama, that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever enters ihram for Hajj or Umra from al-Masjid al-Aqsa to al-Masjid al-Haram, what preceded of his sin and what follows is forgiven, or Paradise is due for him; Abd Allah doubted which of the two he said."
"6931","Al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Kufi narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Abd Allah, from Ibn Judan, from Umm Salama, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called a servant and she delayed, and in his hand was a siwak, so he said: Were it not for retribution I would have struck you with this siwak."
"6932","Umar ibn Shabba Abu Zayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthma narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Yaqub narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Wahb, that his father informed him, from Umm Salama, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to enter upon his wives every morning and greet them, and there was among them a woman who had honey, so when he entered upon her she would present some of it to him, so he would stay with her, and Aisha and Hafsa were jealous of that, so when he entered upon them both they said: O Messenger of Allah, we smell from you the odor of maghafir, he said: So he left that honey."
"6933","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi Aisha, from a freedwoman of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed Fajr then gave salam, said: O Allah, I ask You for beneficial knowledge, good provision, and accepted deed."
"6934","Al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Abu Nasr, from Musawir al-Himyari, from his mother, from Umm Salama, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No hypocrite loves Ali, and no believer hates him."
"6935","Uqba ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Talha ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Umm Kulthum bint Abd Allah ibn Zamaa, that her grandmother Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), handed her a dyeing vessel of brass, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ghusl in this. Talha said: So Umm Kulthum showed it to me; it was about a sa or a little larger."
"6936","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ghundar, narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq, that he heard Abu Salama narrating, from Umm Salama, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not die until most of his prayer was sitting, apart from the obligatory, and the most beloved deed to him was the most persistent even if little."
"6937","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughira, from Umm Musa, from Umm Salama, she said: By Him by Whom oaths are sworn, Ali was indeed the closest of people in last contact with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on the day he died in the house of Aisha, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) morning after morning kept saying: Has Ali come? several times. She said: And I think he had sent him on some need. He said: Then he came later, and we thought he had some need with him, so we left the house and sat by the door, and I was the nearest of them, so Ali leaned over him and kept speaking to him privately and confiding, then he died that very day."
"6938","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn al-Bakhtari al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon us and with me was a boy complaining, so he said: What is wrong with him? We said: We suspect the evil eye for him. So he said: Why do you not perform ruqya for him from the eye?"
"6939","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, from Safina, freedman of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, she said: The general bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his illness was: Prayer and what your right hands possess, until he kept mumbling it in his chest though his tongue could not utter it."
"6940","Abd Allah ibn Muawiya narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Umm Salama, she said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was reclining in my house, he suddenly sat up saying Inna lillahi wa inna ilayhi rajiun, so I said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, what is the matter with you saying istirja? He said: For an army of my umma coming from the direction of Sham heading to the House, for a man whom Allah protects from them, until when they are at al-Bayda of Dhu al-Hulayfa they are swallowed up, though their starting points are various. I said: May my father be sacrificed for you, how are they swallowed up all together while their starting points are various? He said: Among them is one compelled, among them is one compelled, among them is one compelled."
"6941","Abd Allah ibn Muawiya narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Yusuf ibn Sad, from Aisha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"6942","Sulayman ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Murra, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his maternal aunt Umm Salama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who drinks in a silver vessel only gurgles in his belly the fire of Hell."
"6943","Abu Hisham al-Rifai narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abi Abd Allah narrated to us, from Qatada, from Salih Abu al-Khalil, from a companion of his, and sometimes Salih said: from Mujahid, from Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be disagreement at the death of a caliph, so a man of Quraysh from the people of Madina will go out to Makka, then people of Makka will come to him and bring him out while he is unwilling, and they will pledge to him between the Maqam and the Rukn. Then they will send to him an army from Sham, and when they are at al-Bayda they are swallowed up. When people learn of that, the Abdal of Sham and groups from Iraq will come to him and pledge to him. And a man of Quraysh whose maternal uncles are Kalb will arise and send to them a detachment, or he said: an army among whom is their believer, and they will prevail over them. So he will divide their fay among people and act among them by the Sunna of their Prophet, and Islam will lay its side to the ground; he will remain seven years."
"6944","Sufyan ibn Waki narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, meaning from Khalid, from Abu Qilaba, from Zaynab bint Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, she said: My bedding was opposite the prayer place of the Messenger of Allah, and he used to pray while I was opposite him."
"6945","Sufyan ibn Waki narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Dawud, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Judan, from his grandmother, from Umm Salama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu al-Haytham al-Ansari came to him seeking a servant, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) promised him if he obtained captives. Then he met Umar, so he said to him: O Abu al-Haytham, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has obtained captives, so come to him and claim your promise. So Abu al-Haytham and Umar went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu al-Haytham has come to you claiming his promise. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: We have obtained two black boys, choose whichever you wish. He said: I consult you. So he said: The one consulted is trusted; take this, for he has prayed with us, and do not beat him, for we have been forbidden from beating those who pray."
"6946","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj, Hudba ibn Khalid, Hawthara ibn Ashras, Ali ibn al-Jad, and Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abu al-Ushara al-Darimi, from his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, is slaughter only between the throat cavity or the throat? He said: Yes indeed, if you stabbed in its thigh it would suffice you. And in the hadith of Hawthara: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, if you stabbed in its thigh it would suffice you."
"6947","Sufyan ibn Waki narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Abd Allah, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Judan al-Qurashi, from his grandmother, from Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in my house and in his hand was a siwak, so he called a maidservant of his, or hers, until anger became apparent on his face. So Umm Salama went out to the chambers and found the maidservant playing with an animal, so she said: Do I not see you playing with this animal while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) calls you? She said: No, by Him Who sent you with the truth, I did not hear you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for fear of retaliation, I would have hurt you with this siwak."
"6948","Abu al-Husayn al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uzayz narrated to us, he said: Salama informed me, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, he informed him, that Safina, freedman of Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him, that Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell."
"6949","Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Kathir narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Mujalid, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, from Umm Salama, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rakas in my house, so I said to him: What are these two? He said: I used to pray them before Asr."
"6950","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abu Mashar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Aban ibn Uthman, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, he said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting with Aisha behind him, Abu Bakr sought permission and entered, then Umar sought permission and entered, then Ali sought permission and entered, then Sad ibn Malik sought permission and entered, then Uthman ibn Affan sought permission and entered, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was conversing with his knee uncovered, so he extended his garment over his knees and said to his wife: Move back from me. They conversed a while, then left. Aisha said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, your Companions entered upon you and you did not fix your garment, nor did you move me back from you, until Uthman entered? So he said: O Aisha, shall I not be shy of a man of whom the angels are shy? By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the angels are shy of Uthman as they are shy of Allah and His Messenger. Had he entered while you were near me, he would not have raised his head, nor spoken, until he left."
"6951","Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Abi Khidash narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from his father, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, he said: Umm Salama said: When Abu Salama died I said: A stranger, and in a strange land, I shall surely weep for him a weeping that will be talked about. She said: While I was thus preparing to weep for him, a woman from the Saeed came intending to help me weep for him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met her and said to her: Do you want to bring Satan into a house from which Allah has expelled him? So I refrained from weeping."
"6952","Mujahid ibn Musa al-Khuttalli narrated to us, Abu Muawiya narrated to us, Musa ibn Ubayda al-Rabadhi narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Ayyash al-Zuraqi, from Anas ibn Malik, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw what my umma will do after me, so I chose for them intercession on the Day of Resurrection."
"6953","Mujahid narrated to us, Bahz narrated to me, Shuba narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi Aisha, from a freedman of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered morning, said: O Allah, I ask You for beneficial knowledge, good provision, and accepted deed."
"6954","Sahl ibn Zanjala narrated to us, Ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ikrima ibn Ammar, from Uthal ibn Qurra, from Ibn Hawshab al-Hanafi, he said: Umm Salama narrated to me, she said: Fatima bint al-Nabi (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carrying al-Hasan and al-Husayn on her sides, in her hand a pot for al-Hasan containing sakhina, until she brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When she placed it before him he said to her: Where is Abu al-Hasan? She said: In the house. So he called him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Ali, Fatima, al-Hasan and al-Husayn sat eating. Umm Salama said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never invited me to share, nor ever ate food while I was with him, except he invited me before that day, meaning by samani: he invited me to it. When they finished he wrapped them in his garment, then said: O Allah, be hostile to whoever is hostile to them, and befriend whoever befriends them."
"6955","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Khusayf narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Aisha, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing gold, we said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not fasten musk with gold? He said: Why do you not fasten it with silver then smear it with saffron so it becomes like gold?"
"6956","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Ata, from Umm Salama, similar to that."
"6957","Kamil narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Umm Salama, that she saw a relative of hers blowing when he wanted to prostrate, so she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a boy called Rabah: Soil your face."
"6958","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from his father, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, he said: Umm Salama said: When Abu Salama died, I said: A stranger, and in a strange land? I shall surely weep for him a weeping that will be talked about. While I was thus, a woman from the Saeed came, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Do you want to bring Satan into a house from which Allah has expelled him? She said: So I refrained from that."
"6959","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Nabhan, from Umm Salama, she mentioned the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If one of you has a mukatab, and he has what he can pay, let her veil herself from him."
"6960","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Said ibn Abi Said, from Abd Allah ibn Rafi, from Umm Salama, that she said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I am a woman who braids my head tightly, shall I undo it for ghusl of janaba? He said: It suffices you to pour three handfuls of water over it, then pour over it, then you are purified."
"6961","Dawud ibn Amr ibn Zuhayr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from a man of the children of Umm Salama whose name is Salama ibn Umar ibn Abi Salama, he said: Umm Salama said: O Messenger of Allah, why do I not hear Allah mention women regarding migration? So Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed: So their Lord responded to them that I do not waste the deed of any doer among you, male or female, to the end of the verse. Dawud said: Sufyan said: With this verse the Khawarij went out, and with it women went out."
"6962","Dawud narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said: Umm Salama said: O Messenger of Allah, men go to battle and we do not go to battle, and we only have half the inheritance? So Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed: And do not wish for what Allah has favored some of you with over others. He said: And this verse was revealed concerning her: Indeed the Muslim men and Muslim women, and the believing men and believing women, to the end of the verse."
"6963","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Zaynab bint Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting in the house of Umm Salama and with him was a mukhannath sitting, and he said to Abd Allah ibn Abi Umayya, brother of Umm Salama: O Abd Allah, if Allah grants you conquest of Taif tomorrow, I shall point you to the daughter of Ghaylan, a woman of Thaqif, who comes forward with four and goes back with eight. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This one shall not enter upon you."
"6964","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Humayd ibn Nafi, from Zaynab bint Abi Salama, from her mother Umm Salama, and Umm Habiba, wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they both said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my daughter's husband has died, and I fear for her eye, shall I apply kohl to her? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman among you used to throw a dung ball at the head of the year, and it is only four months and ten days."
"6965","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Yahya, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would enter morning junub from women without a dream, then remain fasting."
"6966","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray witr with seven and five, not separating between them with salam nor speech."
"6967","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you attend the sick or the dead, say good, for the angels say amen to what you say. When Abu Salama died I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: How shall I say? He said: Say: O Allah forgive us and him, and grant us from him a good succession. So I said it, and Allah the Mighty and Majestic granted me Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after him."
"6968","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Umm Salama, she said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Hisham ibn al-Mughira used to maintain kinship, honor guests, free captives, and feed food, and had he lived he would have accepted Islam; will that benefit him? He said: No, he used to give for the world and its mention and praise, and he never once said: My Lord forgive me on the Day of Recompense."
"6969","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Hassan ibn Mukhariq, he said: Umm Salama said: A daughter of mine complained, so I prepared nabidh for her in a jug, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered while it was fermenting, so he said: What is this? I said: My daughter complained so we prepared this for her. So he said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic has not placed your cure in what is forbidden."
"6970","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from al-Marur ibn Suwayd, from Umm al-Muminin Umm Salama, she said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about those transformed, will they have offspring? So he said: No one transformed ever had offspring nor progeny."
"6971","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mughira, from Umm Musa, she said: Umm Salama said: By Whom Umm Salama swears, Ali was indeed the closest of people in last contact with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said to her: It was the morning he died, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to him, and he was, I think, sent on some need. She said: Morning after morning he kept saying: Has Ali come? three times. She said: Then he came before sunrise, and when he came we knew he had some need with him, so we left the house, and we had visited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the house of Aisha. She said: I was the last to leave the house, then I sat nearest of them to the door, so Ali leaned over him, and he was the last of people in contact with him, and kept speaking to him privately and confiding."
"6972","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salama, she said: The most beloved deed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was that which was persisted in even if little."
"6973","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Salim, from Abu Salama, from Umm Salama, she said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fast a month, except he would join Shaban with Ramadan."
"6974","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib, from Wahb, freedman of Abu Ahmad, from Umm Salama, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her while she was veiling, so he said: One wrap, not two."
"6975","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Ibn Sabit, from Hafsa bint Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your women are a tillage for you, so come to your tillage as you wish. He said: One opening, one opening."
"6976","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Abu Salama narrating from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not die until most of his prayer was while sitting, and the most beloved deed to Allah the Mighty and Majestic was what the servant persists in even if slight."
"6977","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Abu Salama, from Umm Salama, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The legs of the minbar are watering places in Paradise."
"6978","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abu Qilaba, from Zaynab bint Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, she said: My bedding was by the prayer place of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he used to pray while I was opposite him."
"6979","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, from Zaynab bint Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, that she arrived while ill, and mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Circumambulate behind the people while riding. She said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while at the Kaba, reciting al-Tur."
"6980","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Nafi, from Safiyya bint Abi Ubayd, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hem of women is a span. I said: O Messenger of Allah, then her feet will come out? He said: Then a cubit, they do not exceed it."
"6981","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he, Ibn Abbas, and Abu Hurayra discussed the woman whose husband dies while she is pregnant. Abu Salama said: So I said: When she delivers she is lawful. Ibn Abbas said: Her lawfulness is at the later of the two terms. Abu Hurayra said: I am with the son of my brother, meaning Abu Salama. So they sent Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas, to Umm Salama and asked her about that. So Umm Salama said: Subaya bint al-Harith al-Aslamiyya delivered nights after the death of her husband, then a man of Banu Abd al-Dar surnamed Abu al-Sanabil proposed to her, and informed her that she had become lawful, and she wanted to marry another. So Abu al-Sanabil said to her: You have not become lawful. So Subaya came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so he commanded her to marry."
"6982","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu al-Khalil, from Safina, from Umm Salama, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while dying, kept saying: Prayer and what your right hands possess. He kept saying it though his tongue could not utter it."
"6983","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Dabba ibn Mihsan, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be rulers whom you recognize and deny. Whoever denies has been absolved, and whoever dislikes has been safe, but whoever is pleased and follows. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not fight them? He said: No, so long as they pray the five for you."
"6984","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umara narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from an umm walad of Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, she said: I used to drag my hem, passing by filthy places and clean places, so I asked Umm Salama about that, so she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: What comes after it purifies it."
"6985","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Hunayda al-Khuzai, from his mother, she said: I entered upon Umm Salama and asked her about fasting, so she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command me to fast three days of every month, the first of them Monday and Thursday and Monday."
"6986","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Hind bint al-Harith, from Umm Salama, that she said: Women in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he gave salam from the obligatory prayer, would stand, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and whoever prayed behind him of men remained. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, the men stood."
"6987","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Thabit ibn Umara informed us, he said: Rayta narrated to me, from Kabsha bint Abi Maryam, that they asked Umm Salama about drinks, she said: I narrate to you what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid his family from: he used to forbid us from mixing dates and raisins, and from cooking pits."
"6988","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ibn Yusuf informed us, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Umm Salama, that she said: I brought near to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a roasted side, so he ate it, then went out and prayed without performing wudu."
"6989","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Muadh ibn Muadh al-Anbari narrated to us, Abu Kab, the silk merchant, narrated to us, he said: Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to me, he said: I asked Umm Salama, I said: O Mother of the Believers, what was the most frequent supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he was with you? She said: His most frequent supplication was: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. She said: So I said to him: O Messenger of Allah, how frequent is your supplication: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. He said: O Umm Salama, there is no human except his heart is between two fingers of the fingers of Allah; what He wills He keeps upright, and what He wills He causes to deviate."
"6990","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abu Asim al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Sayfi, he said: Ikrima ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham informed me, that Umm Salama informed him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) swore he would not enter upon some of his wives for a month, and when it was twenty-nine days he came morning or evening. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, you swore not to enter. He said: The month is twenty-nine days."
"6991","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ibn Uyayna and Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Hind bint al-Harith, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one night and said: Glory be to Allah, what trials Allah has sent down, and what treasures He has opened. Wake the occupants of the chambers, for many clothed in this world will be naked on the Day of Resurrection. Ismail said in his hadith: So I saw Hind make buttons for the sleeves of her shirt."
"6992","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, he said: A woman of the earlier women would make buttons for the sleeve of her shirt, placing it on her finger, covering the ring with it."
"6993","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The transgressing party will kill Ammar."
"6994","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, I think from Hisham al-Dastuwai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salama, from Zaynab bint Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, she said: While I was lying with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I menstruated, so I slipped away and took my menstrual clothes. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Have you menstruated? I said: Yes. So he called me and I lay with him in the blanket. She said: She and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ghusl from one vessel, and he used to kiss her while fasting."
"6995","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, he said: Umm Salama said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was quicker in hastening Zuhr than you, and you are quicker in hastening Asr than him."
"6996","Abu Khaythama informed us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Rafi, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When supper is present and prayer is present, begin with supper."
"6997","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: My father informed me, from Zaynab bint Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: You dispute to me, and perhaps one of you is more eloquent in his plea than another, and I am only human. So whomever I judge for something of his brother's right, I only cut for him a piece of the Fire, so let him not take it."
"6998","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Abu Yunus narrated to us, he said: Muhajir ibn al-Qibtiyya narrated to me that he heard Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An army invading this House will surely be swallowed up in a desert of the earth."
"6999","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from his father, from Umm Salama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he married Umm Salama, stayed with her three days, then said: You are not despised by your family; if you wish I shall stay seven for you, and if I stay seven for you I shall stay seven for my wives."
"7000","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Abi Aisha narrated to me, he said: A freedman of Umm Salama narrated to me, he said: I heard Umm Salama say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed Fajr, said: O Allah, I ask You for beneficial knowledge, accepted deed, and good provision."
"7001","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, he said: Nafi informed me, from Zayd ibn Abd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The one who drinks in silver vessels only gurgles in his belly the fire of Hell."
"7002","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Amir, brother of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would enter morning junub, then fast."
"7003","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from his father, from Zaynab bint Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded her to attend the Fajr prayer on the day of sacrifice at Makka."
"7004","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abu Muawiya narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Zaynab bint Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, she said: Umm Habiba came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, do you want my sister? He said: What shall I do with her? She said: Marry her. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: And do you like that? She said: So I said: Yes, I am not secluding you to myself, and the most deserving to share me in good is my sister. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: She is not lawful to me. She said: By Allah, it has reached me that you are proposing Durra bint Umm Salama. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had she been lawful I would not have married her, for Thuwayba, freedwoman of Banu Hashim, nursed me and her father, so do not present to me your daughters nor your sisters."
"7005","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubayda al-Rabadhi, from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Ayyash al-Zuraqi, from Anas ibn Malik, from Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was shown what my umma will do after me, so I chose for them intercession until the Day of Resurrection."
"7006","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Umm Salama: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf entered upon her and said: O mother, I fear my abundant wealth will destroy me; I am the wealthiest of Quraysh. She said: O my son, spend, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Among my Companions is one who will not see me after I part from him. So Abd al-Rahman went out and met Umar and informed him of what Umm Salama said. So Umar came and entered upon her and said: By Allah, am I among them? She said: No, and I shall not absolve anyone after you."
"7007","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Zaynab bint Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, she said: Umm Sulaym came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. He said: When she sees water let her perform ghusl. So I said: You have disgraced women; does a woman have a wet dream? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May your right hand be soiled, then in what does her child resemble her?"
"7008","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, Abu Awn Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayra say: Perform wudu from what fire has touched. He said: So Marwan sent to Umm Salama and asked her, so she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nibbled a shoulder with me, then went out to prayer without touching water."
"7009","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Abi Thabit informed me, that Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Amr, and al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, informed him, that they both heard Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham informing that Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him, that when she arrived at Madina she informed them she was the daughter of Abu Umayya ibn al-Mughira, so they disbelieved her, saying: How lying are strangers! Until some of them set out for Hajj, so they said: Will you write to your family? So she wrote with them. They returned to Madina believing her, so she increased in honor with them. She said: When I delivered Zaynab, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me proposing to me, so I said: One like me married? I have no child in me, and I am jealous with dependents. He said: I am older than you, and as for jealousy Allah will remove it, and as for dependents, to Allah and to His Messenger. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her. He kept coming to her saying: Where is Zunab, until Ammar came and snatched her, saying: This one prevents the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she was nursing her. Then he came to her and said: Where is Zunab? So Qariba bint Abi Umayya said, and she was in agreement with her: Ibn Yasir took her. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall come to you tonight. She said: So I put out my clothes and took out grains of barley that were in my jar and took out fat and made asida for him. She said: He spent the night, then morning came. So he said when morning came: You have honor with your family; if you wish I shall stay seven for you, and if I stay seven for you I shall stay seven for my wives."
"7010","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke from his sleep saying istirja. She said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the matter with you? He said: A group of my umma will be swallowed up, sent to a man; he comes to Makka and Allah protects him from them, and they are swallowed up; their place of perishing is one though their starting points are various. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how is their place of perishing one while their starting points are various? He said: Among them is one compelled, so he comes compelled."
"7011","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to me, from his father, from Zaynab bint Abi Salama, from her mother Umm Salama, she said: I said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, is there reward for me regarding the sons of Abu Salama? I spend on them, and they are my sons and I shall not leave them thus and thus. Saying: Whether there is reward for me or not. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Yes, for you regarding them is reward for whatever you spend on them."
"7012","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Sulayman ibn Suhaym, freedman of Al Hunayn, narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Abi Sufyan al-Akhnasi, from his mother Umm Hakim bint Umayya ibn al-Akhnas, from Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever enters ihram from al-Masjid al-Aqsa for Umra and for Hajj, what preceded of his sin is forgiven. He said: So Umm Hakim rode for that hadith to Bayt al-Maqdis until she entered ihram from it for Umra."
"7013","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Hind bint al-Harith informed me, from Umm Salama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he gave salam, the women would stand when he finished his salam, and he would remain a little. Muhammad said: So we think, and Allah knows best, that his remaining was so that women would leave before those who departed of the people could reach them."
"7014","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywa and Ibn Lahia narrated to us, they said: We heard Yazid ibn Abi Habib say: Abu Imran narrated to me, that he performed Hajj with his freedmen, so I came to Umm Salama, Mother of the Believers, and said: O Mother of the Believers, I have never performed Hajj; with which shall I begin: Umra or Hajj? She said: Begin with whichever you wish. He said: Then I came to Safiyya, Mother of the Believers, and asked her, and she said to me like what Umm Salama said to me. He said: Then I came to Umm Salama and informed her of Safiyya's saying, so Umm Salama said to me: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O family of Muhammad, whoever of you performs Hajj, let him enter ihram for Umra in Hajj, or in his Hajj."
"7015","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to me, Budayl narrated to me, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from Safiyya bint Shayba, from Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A woman whose husband has died shall not wear saffron-dyed garments, nor striped garments, nor jewelry, nor dye, nor apply kohl."
"7016","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Bajali narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Abu Abd Allah al-Jadali, he said: Umm Salama said: Is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reviled on the pulpits? I said: And how is that? She said: Is not Ali reviled and whoever loves him? So I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved him."
"7017","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abd al-Mumin ibn Khalid al-Hanafi al-Khurasani narrated to us, he said: I met him at Marw, Abd Allah ibn Burayda al-Aslami narrated to us from Umm Salama, she said: No garment was more beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than shirts."
"7018","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salama, he said: Umm Salama said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his blanket, and I felt what women feel, so I slipped out of the blanket. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you menstruated? I said: Yes. He said: That is what has been decreed upon the daughters of Adam. So I tended to my affair then returned. So he said: Come and enter with me. She said: So I entered with him in the blanket."
"7019","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Zaida narrated to us, Ammar ibn Abi Muawiya al-Bajali narrated to us, from Abu Salama, he said: Umm Salama narrated to me that she used to perform ghusl, she and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from janaba in one vessel."
"7020","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaida narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while his face was pale. She said: So I thought that was from pain. I said: O Messenger of Allah, why is your face pale? He said: Because of the seven dinars we hid yesterday; we eveninged and did not distribute them, and they are in the side of the bedding."
"7021","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from some children of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on a khumra."
"7022","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Buhlul ibn Muwarriq al-Shami narrated to us, Musa ibn Ubayda narrated to us, he said: Thabit, freedman of Umm Salama, informed me, from Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he left his house, prayed two rakas before Zuhr, and prayed two rakas before Asr. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a collector to a people, and when it reached them some of them wanted to help him and prepared for that. When the collector arrived and saw the people, he thought they would kill him, so he returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: They denied me their charity. And the collector was detained with the people, so they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) excusing themselves to him, and he had finished Zuhr prayer. They kept excusing themselves to him until he prayed Asr, and he forgot the two rakas he used to pray before Asr. So Aisha sent to Umm Salama: O my sister, what are the two rakas the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in your chamber after Asr? So she informed her, and said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray before it nor after it."
"7023","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Habban ibn Hilal narrated to us, Harun al-Qari narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Shahr, from Umm Salama, she said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this verse, so he said: Indeed it is a deed not righteous."
"7024","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Asadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salama, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) covered Ali, Hasan, Husayn and Fatima with a cloak, then said: O Allah, these are my Ahl al-Bayt and my close kin; O Allah, remove from them impurity and purify them thoroughly. So Umm Salama said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, am I among them? He said: You are toward good."
"7025","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulayka, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he recited, would cut his recitation verse by verse: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Merciful. All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds. Master of the Day of Judgment."
"7026","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Shuja ibn al-Walid ibn Qays narrated to us, from Ali ibn Abd al-Ala, from Abu Sahl, from Mussa al-Azdiyya, from Umm Salama, she said: A postpartum woman in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sit forty days, and we would smear our faces with wars for melasma."
"7027","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Awf ibn al-Harith, from his sister Rumaytha bint al-Harith, from Umm Salama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not hurt me regarding Aisha, for by Allah, revelation does not descend upon me while I am in the blanket of any woman among you except Aisha. I said: Certainly, by Allah, I shall never hurt you regarding her."
"7028","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, Darraj narrated to us, from al-Saib, freedman of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best prayer of women is in the innermost of their houses."
"7029","Repeated: Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salama, she said: On the day of al-Khandaq, while he was handing them milk and his hair had become dusty, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: By Allah I have not forgotten, while he was saying: To the Ansar and the Muhajira. She said: Then Ammar entered, so he said: Woe to you, or woe to him, the transgressing party will kill him."
"7030","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Fatima: Bring me your husband and your two daughters. She said: So she brought them, and he cast over them a Fadak cloak, then placed his hand over them and said: O Allah, these are the family of Muhammad, so place Your prayers and blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. Umm Salama said: So I lifted the cloak to enter it, and he pulled it from my hand and said: You are upon good."
"7031","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab al-Ukli narrated to us, he said: Usama ibn Zayd informed me, he said: Abd Allah ibn Rafi narrated to me, he said: I heard Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then two men came disputing about matters that had become effaced and vanished. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I only judge between you in a matter about which nothing has been revealed to me. Whomever I judge for with a plea that I see, and I thereby cut from his brother's wealth, he only cuts thereby a piece of the Fire, a brand on his neck on the Day of Resurrection. So the two men wept and said: O Messenger of Allah, my right that I seek is for my brother. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, but go, divide and aim for what is right, then let each one of you absolve his companion."
"7032","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, from Dhakwan, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Asr, then entered my house and prayed two rakas. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you prayed a prayer you did not use to pray? So he said: Wealth came to me and distracted me from two rakas I used to bow after Zuhr, so I prayed them now. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we make them up when missed? He said: No."
"7033","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl, from Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ali, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hajj is the jihad of every weak one."
"7034","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilaba, from Qabisa ibn Dhuayb, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Abu Salama while his sight had fixed upward, so he closed it, then said: When the soul is seized the sight follows it. So people of his family clamored. So he said: Do not supplicate against yourselves except with good, for the angels say amen to what you say. Then he said: O Allah forgive Abu Salama, raise his rank among the guided, succeed him in his offspring among those who remain, forgive us and him, O Lord of the worlds. O Allah expand for him in his grave, and illumine for him in his grave."
"7035","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, Darraj narrated to us, from al-Saib, freedman of Umm Salama, that women of Hims entered upon Umm Salama, so she asked them: From whom are you? They said: From the people of Hims. So she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any woman who removes her clothes in other than her house, Allah removes a veil from her."
"7036","Hadith of Hafsa, Mother of the Believers, may Allah be pleased with her. 1 - With the same chain he said: Abu al-Qasim Zahir ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed us, Abu Sa'd Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Janzarudhi informed us, recited to him while I listened, twice: once in Jumada al-Ula in the year 451, and once in Jumada al-Akhira of the same year, and Shaykh Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Hamdun al-Sulami, recited to him on the first of Sha'ban in the year 453, recited by Shaykh Abu Salih al-Mu'adhdhin, may Allah have mercy on him, both said: Abu Amr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan informed us, al-Janzarudhi said with the recitation of Abu Ja'far al-Aza'imi in Rajab in the year 375, and he acknowledged it and said: yes, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma, nephew of Juwayriya, narrated to us, Juwayriya narrated to us, from Nafi', from Abdullah, from Hafsa, Mother of the Believers, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rak'as when dawn broke."
"7037","2 - Abdullah narrated to us, Juwayriya narrated to us, from Nafi', that Safiyya bint Abi Ubayd narrated to him from Hafsa, or from A'isha, or from both of them, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day, or who believes in Allah and His Messenger, to mourn over a dead person for more than three days, except over her husband."
"7038","3 - Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdala, from Sawa', from Hafsa, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he went to his bed, would lie on his right side and say: My Lord, protect me from Your punishment on the Day You resurrect Your servants."
"7039","4 - Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abda narrated to us, from Abdullah, from Nafi', from Safiyya bint Abi Ubayd, from Hafsa bint Umar, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead person for more than three days, except over a husband."
"7040","5 - Abu Talib Abd al-Jabbar ibn Asim narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Hafsa bint Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the mu'adhdhin called the adhan for Fajr, would stand and pray the two rak'as of Fajr, then go out to the mosque, and food became forbidden; he said: and he would not call the adhan until morning came."
"7041","6 - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'ida, from Asim, from al-Musayyab, from Hafsa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast Mondays and Thursdays."
"7042","7 - Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Harb narrated to us, Shayban Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, Abu Ya'fur al-Abdi narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Sa'id, from Hafsa, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning Uthman: Shall I not feel shy before a man before whom the angels feel shy."
"7043","8 - Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that Hafsa said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed Jumu'a, would enter her house and pray two rak'as."
"7044","9 - Isma'il ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn al-Hasan ibn Bukayr al-Thaqafi al-Raqqi narrated to me, Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Abi Karima, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from Hafsa, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Nothing brings out the Dajjal except a fit of anger he becomes angry with."
"7045","10 - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Ashja'i narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays, from al-Hurr ibn al-Sayyah, from Hunayda ibn Khalid, from Hafsa, she said: There were four things the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not leave: fasting the day of Ashura, the ten days, three days of every month, and the two rak'as before the morning prayer."
"7046","11 - Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Zurara al-Kufi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Za'ida narrated to us, from Abu Ayyub, from Asim, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi' and Ma'bad, from Haritha ibn Wahb al-Khuza'i, he said: Hafsa, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to assign his right hand for his food, and assign his left hand for everything else."
"7047","12 - Harun ibn Abdullah al-Bazzaz narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Umayya ibn Safwan, he heard his grandfather say: Hafsa narrated to me that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An army seeking this House will surely come to it intending to raid it, until when they are in a desert land, their middle will be swallowed up, then their first and last will call out and all of them will be swallowed, and none will escape except the lone fugitive who informs about them. Sufyan said: Then a man stood up to Umayya and said: I testify against you that you did not lie about your grandfather, and I testify about your grandfather that he did not lie about Hafsa, and I testify about Hafsa that she did not lie about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7048","13 - al-Hasan ibn Shabib, a Baghdadi, narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, from Umm Mubashshir, from Hafsa, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I hope that no one who witnessed Badr and al-Hudaybiyya, Allah willing, will enter the Fire. She said: I said: Does not Allah Almighty say: There is none of you but will come to it; this is upon your Lord a decree decreed. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you not hear Him say: Then We will save those who feared Allah and leave the wrongdoers therein on their knees."
"7049","14 - Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Hafsa, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she was sitting with A'isha in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I wish some of my Companions were with me so we could talk. A'isha said: Send for Abu Bakr to talk with you. He said: No. Hafsa said: Send for Umar to talk with you. He said: No, but send for Uthman. So Uthman came and entered, and the two of them stood and let down the curtain. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Uthman: You will be killed as a martyr, so be patient, may Allah grant you patience, and do not take off a shirt with which Allah Almighty has clothed you for twelve years and six months, until you meet Allah while He is pleased with you. Uthman said: If the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for me for patience, he said: O Allah, grant him patience. Then Uthman went out, and when he turned away, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah grant you patience, for you will be martyred and die while fasting, and you will break your fast with me."
"7050","15 - Ibrahim said: And my father narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, that A'isha narrated to him the like of that."
"7051","16 - Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hammad said: Asim informed us, from Sawa', brother of Mughith, from Hafsa, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast three days of the month: Monday, Thursday, and Monday of the following week."
"7052","17 - Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Ashja'i, and he is not Ubaydullah, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays, from al-Hurr ibn al-Sayyah, from Hunayda ibn Khalid al-Khuza'i, from Hafsa, she said: There were four things the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not leave: fasting the ten days, Ashura, fasting three days of every month, and two rak'as before the morning prayer."
"7053","18 - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Ashja'i narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays, and he did not mention in it what his son mentioned."
"7054","19 - Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Hafsa, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to end our state with an Umra, I said: O Messenger of Allah, what prevents you from ending it with us? He said: I have matted my hair and garlanded my sacrificial animal, so I will not end it until I slaughter."
"7055","20 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Shutayr ibn Shakl, from Hafsa bint Umar, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting."
"7056","21 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Hafsa, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to end with an Umra, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, what prevents you from ending it? He said: I have brought a sacrificial animal and matted my hair."
"7057","22 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Nafi', from Safiyya bint Abi Ubayd, from Hafsa bint Umar, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and His Messenger, or who believes in Allah and the Last Day, to mourn over a dead person for more than three days, except over a husband."
"7058","23 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, he said: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn Umar, he said: Hafsa informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two light prostrations when dawn broke."
"7059","24 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Malik, from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, from al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wada'a, from Hafsa, she said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray voluntary prayer sitting until a year before his death; he would pray sitting, reciting the sura and prolonging it until it was longer than longer than it."
"7060","25 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Hafsa, that she said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Why have you not ended your Umra? He said: I have matted my hair and garlanded my sacrificial animal, so I will not end it until I slaughter."
"7061","26 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: I saw in a dream as if in my hand was a piece of silk brocade, and I did not point with it to any place in Paradise except that it flew with me to it. He said: Hafsa narrated it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Your brother is a righteous man, or: Abdullah is a righteous man."
"7062","27 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Sawa' al-Khuza'i, from Hafsa bint Umar, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he went to his bed, would place his right hand under his cheek and say: My Lord, protect me from Your punishment on the Day You resurrect Your servants, three times."
"7063","28 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdala, from Sawa', from Hafsa, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast three days of the month: Monday, Thursday, and Monday of the following week."
"7064","29 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us, Ibn Abi Za'ida narrated to us, Abu Ayyub al-Ifriqi narrated to us, from Asim, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi' and Ma'bad, from Haritha ibn Wahb, he said: Hafsa, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to assign his right hand for his food and drink, and assign his left hand for everything else."
"7065","30 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Rawh ibn Aslam narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub and Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', that Ibn Umar saw Ibn Sa'id in one of the streets of Madina, so Ibn Umar reviled him and attacked him, and he swelled until he blocked the road. Then Ibn Umar struck him with a stick and he subsided until he returned, then he swelled until he blocked the road, then Ibn Umar struck him with a stick he had until he broke it over him. Hafsa said to him: What is the matter with you and him? What makes you so attached to him? Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Dajjal only comes out of an anger he becomes angry with."
"7066","31 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Jabbar al-Khattabi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Hafsa, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the mu'adhdhin called the adhan, would pray two rak'as, and food became forbidden, and he would not call the adhan until dawn broke."
"7067","32 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, Ja'far narrated to us, Nafi' narrated to us, that Abdullah ibn Umar informed him that Hafsa said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to end my state during his Hajj which he performed."
"7068","Hadith of Juwayriya bint al-Harith. 1 - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Shababa narrated to us, from Shu'ba, from Qatada, from Abu Ayyub al-Ataki, from Juwayriya, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her while she was fasting on Friday, and said to her: Did you fast yesterday? She said: No. He said: Will you fast tomorrow? She said: No. He said: Then break your fast."
"7069","2 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Ayyub, from Juwayriya, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"7070","3 - Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Abu Ayyub, from Juwayriya bint al-Harith, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her while she was fasting on Friday and said: Did you fast yesterday? She said: No. He said: Do you intend to fast tomorrow? She said: No. He said: Then break your fast."
"7071","4 - Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, from Juwayriya bint al-Harith, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me and said: Is there any food? She said: No, except a bone given to our freedwoman from charity. He said: Bring it near, for it has reached its proper place."
"7072","5 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, freedman of the family of Talha, he said: I heard Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas, narrating from Ibn Abbas, from Juwayriya bint al-Harith, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me in the morning while I was glorifying Allah, then he left for his need, then he returned near midday and said: Have you remained sitting? She said: I said: Yes. He said: Shall I not teach you words which, if weighed against them, would outweigh them, or if measured against them, would outweigh them, meaning against all that you glorified: Glory be to Allah as many as His creation, three times; glory be to Allah as heavy as His Throne, three times; glory be to Allah as pleasing as Himself, three times; glory be to Allah as much as the ink of His words, three times."
"7073","Hadith of Safiyya, Mother of the Believers. 1 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salama, from Abu Idris, from Ibn Safwan, from Safiyya, Mother of the Believers, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will not cease raiding this House until an army raids it; when they are in a desert land, their first and last will be swallowed up, and their middle will not escape. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what about the one coerced among them? He said: Allah will raise them according to what is in their hearts."
"7074","Hadith of Salma bint Qays from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 1 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Salit ibn Ayyub narrated to me, from his mother, from Salma, and she was one of the maternal aunts of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she had prayed with him toward the two qiblas, and she was one of the women of Banu Adi ibn al-Najjar, she said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge allegiance to him among women of the Ansar. When he stipulated upon us that we associate nothing with Allah, and that we not steal, nor commit adultery, nor kill our children, nor bring slander which we fabricate between our hands and feet, nor disobey him in what is right, he said: And that you not deceive your husbands. She said: So we pledged allegiance to him, then we left. I said to a woman among them: Go back and ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what deceiving our husbands is. She said: So she asked him, and he said: She takes his wealth and favors another with it."
"7075","Hadith of Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith. 1 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, from his mother Umm al-Fadl, that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting in Maghrib: By those sent forth in succession."
"7076","2 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Umm al-Fadl, she said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in my house, and said: I had a wife, then I married another wife over her, and my first wife claimed that she suckled the younger one once or twice. He said: One suckling or two sucklings do not make unlawful."
"7077","3 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from Umayr, freedman of Umm al-Fadl, from Umm al-Fadl, that they disputed about the fasting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Arafa, so I sent to him a vessel of milk and he drank."
"7078","4 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from Qabus ibn Abi al-Mukhariq, from Umm al-Fadl, she said: I saw as if in my house there was a piece of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I was distressed by that, so I mentioned that to him. He said: Good, Allah willing; Fatima will give birth to a boy whom you will nurse with the milk of your son Qutham. She said: So she gave birth to Hasan, and she gave him to me and I nursed him. Then I brought him and seated him in his lap, and he urinated on him, so I struck between his shoulders. He said: Be gentle, may Allah keep you right, or may Allah have mercy on you; you have hurt my son. She said: I said: Take off your waist-wrapper and wear another garment until I wash it. He said: Only the urine of a girl is washed, and the urine of a boy is sprinkled with water."
"7079","5 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Husayn ibn Abdullah informed me, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, from Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw Umm Habiba while she was just past weaning, and said: If this little daughter of Abbas lives while I am alive, I will surely marry her."
"7080","6 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, al-Mufaddal ibn Faddala narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had narrated to me that Hind bint al-Harith narrated to him from Umm al-Fadl ibn Abbas, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon his uncle while he was ill, wishing for death because of his sickness. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck the chest of Abbas with his hand, then said: Do not wish for death, O uncle of the Messenger of Allah; if you remain, you will increase in good, and that is good for you, and if you remain, you may seek pardon for something, and that is good for you."
"7081","Hadith of Khadija bint Khuwaylid, may Allah be pleased with her, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 1 - Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Sahl ibn Ziyad al-Harbi, a Basran, trustworthy, narrated to us, he said: Al-Azraq ibn Qays narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Nawfal, or from Abdullah ibn Burayda, Sahl doubted, from Khadija bint Khuwaylid, she said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I said: By my father, where are my children from you? He said: In Paradise. She said: And I asked him, where are my children from my polytheist husbands? He said: In the Fire. I said: Without deeds? He said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"7082","Hadith of Maymuna, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 1 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymuna, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a mouse that fell into ghee and died. He said: Throw it away and what is around it, and eat it."
"7083","2 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymuna: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a dead sheep and said: Why did they not take its hide, tan it, and benefit from it? They said: It is dead. He said: Only eating it was forbidden."
"7084","3 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas; Maymuna informed him that she used to bathe with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from one vessel."
"7085","4 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Manbudh, from his mother, she said: I was with Maymuna, and Ibn Abbas entered upon her. She said: O my son, why do I see your hair unkempt? He said: Umm Ammar, my hairdresser, is menstruating. She said: O my son, what does menstruation have to do with the hand? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would enter upon one of us while she was menstruating and place his head in her lap while she was menstruating, and one of us would bring him his prayer mat and spread it while she was menstruating. O my son, what does menstruation have to do with the hand."
"7086","5 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, he said: Maymuna said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would touch women while they were menstruating, ordering them to wrap themselves in waist-wrappers."
"7087","6 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ziyad ibn Amr ibn Hind, from Imran ibn Hudhayfa, he said: Maymuna used to borrow and borrow much. Her family spoke to her about that and blamed her. She said: I will not stop, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no one who borrows a debt, and Allah Almighty knows that he intends to repay it, except that Allah pays it for him in this world."
"7088","7 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from his maternal aunt Maymuna, she said: A lizard was gifted to us. She said: Two men of her people came to her, so she ordered it to be prepared, then she offered it to them. She said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me while they were eating, and he welcomed them, then he began to eat. When he took a morsel to his mouth, he said: What is this? She said: A lizard gifted to us. She said: So he put down the morsel, and the two men wanted to throw what was in their mouths. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not do that; you, people of Najd, eat it, and we, people of Tihama, dislike it."
"7089","8 - Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, Hanzala al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal narrating that Maymuna said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rak'as before Asr. She said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed a prayer, liked to persist in it."
"7090","9 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Farqad, from Abdullah ibn Malik ibn Hudhafa, from his mother al-Aliya, from Maymuna, she said: Men of Quraysh passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dragging a sheep. He said: Why did you not benefit from its hide? They said: It is dead. He said: Water and qaraz purify it."
"7091","10 - al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Umar ibn Ishaq, that he heard Ata ibn Yasar narrating from Maymuna, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty said: Whoever harms a wali of Mine has deserved My war. No servant draws near to Me with anything like performing My obligations, and he draws near to Me with voluntary acts until I love him. When I love him, I become his leg with which he walks, his hand with which he grasps, his tongue with which he speaks, and his heart with which he understands. If he asks Me, I give him; if he calls upon Me, I answer him. I have never hesitated about anything I do as I hesitate about his death; that is because he dislikes it and I dislike harming him."
"7092","11 - Abu Musa Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Harawi narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Abi Sawda, from his brother, from Maymuna, she said: O Messenger of Allah, give us a ruling about Bayt al-Maqdis. He said: It is the land of gathering and the land of resurrection. Go to it and pray in it, for a prayer in it is like a thousand prayers. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what of one who cannot bear the journey to it? He said: Whoever cannot come to it, let him gift to it oil to be lit in it; whoever gifts oil to it is like one who has come to it."
"7093","12 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm al-Antaki narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Nudba, freedwoman of Maymuna, from Maymuna, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would touch a woman among his wives while she was menstruating, with a cloth over her reaching to the middle of the thighs."
"7094","13 - Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from his maternal aunt Maymuna bint al-Harith, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on a khumra."
"7095","14 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ar'ara narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrating from Muhammad ibn Abdullah, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi', from Maymuna, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: My nation will remain in good, its affair held together, as long as children of adultery do not appear among them; when they appear, I fear that Allah will envelop them with punishment."
"7096","15 - Muhammad ibn al-Minhal, brother of Hajjaj al-Anmati, narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid, meaning Ibn Ziyad, narrated to us, Sulayman al-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Shaddad narrated to me from Maymuna, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he wanted to touch a woman among his wives while she was menstruating, would order her to wrap herself in a waist-wrapper."
"7097","16 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Furat, and he is Ibn Dinar al-Tahi, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsa, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymuna, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke up gloomy, then evening came while he was so, then morning came while he was so. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, why do I see you gloomy? He said: Gabriel, peace be upon him, promised to come to me, and he never broke his promise to me. She said: So they looked, and there was a puppy under their couch. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that place to be washed with water. She said: And Gabriel, peace be upon him, came to him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: You promised to come to me and you never broke your promise to me. Gabriel, peace be upon him, said to him: Do you not know that we do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image."
"7098","17 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Umar ibn Ishaq ibn Yasar narrated to us, he said: I read to Ata a book with him, and in it was: Maymuna, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to me that she said: O Messenger of Allah, does a man take off his khuffs every hour? He said: No, but let him wipe over them as long as he wishes."
"7099","18 - Muhammad ibn Qudama narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, he said: al-Shaybani narrated to me from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Maymuna, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in a cloak, part of it on him and part of it on her, while she was menstruating."
"7100","19 - Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us, Marwan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah al-Amiri, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Maymuna, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I heard her say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prostrated, would spread his arms until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen from behind him, and when he sat, he would settle upon his left thigh."
"7101","20 - Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah, nephew of Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from his uncle, from his maternal aunt Maymuna, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prostrated, if an animal wished, it could pass under his hands."
"7102","21 - Abu Amir Abdullah ibn Amir narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Saluli narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymuna, she said: I and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became ritually impure, so I bathed from a basin, and some remained in it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to bathe from it, and I said: I have already bathed from it. He said: Water does not become ritually impure."
"7103","22 - al-Zimmani narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, al-Muthanna narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, freedman of Maymuna, from Maymuna, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This world is sweet and green. Whoever is God-fearing in it and reforms, otherwise he is like one who eats and is never satiated. People are as distant as the two stars: one rises from the east, and the other sets in the west."
"7104","23 - Ishaq narrated to us, he said: I heard Sufyan in Mina saying: I memorized it from the mouth of al-Zuhri, narrating from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymuna, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a sheep belonging to her freedwoman, which she had been given from charity, and said: Why did they not take its hide, tan it, and benefit from it. They said: O Messenger of Allah, it is dead. He said: Only eating it was forbidden. Abu Ya'qub said: And Sufyan excelled with this verse: Say, I find not in what was revealed to me anything forbidden to one who eats thereof. Sufyan said: If there were nothing but this verse, I would argue with it about corrupt eating."
"7105","24 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Kurayb; Ibn Abbas narrated to us from his maternal aunt, she said: I placed washing water for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he bathed from ritual impurity. He poured the vessel with his left hand onto his right, washed his palms three times, then poured water over his private parts and washed them, then rubbed his hand on the wall or on the ground, then rinsed his mouth and nose, washed his face and forearms, poured water over his head, then poured over the rest of his body, then moved aside and washed his feet. I brought him a cloth, and he gestured with his hand thus, meaning he refused it."
"7106","25 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Burqan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Maymuna, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prostrated, would separate his arms until one behind him could see the whiteness of his armpits."
"7107","26 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Maymuna, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not make nabidh in gourds, nor in jars, nor in pitched vessels; and every drink that intoxicates is forbidden."
"7108","27 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Habib, freedman of Urwa, from Nudba, freedman of Maymuna, from Maymuna, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would touch a woman among his wives while she was menstruating, when she wore a waist-wrapper reaching to the middle of the thighs or the knees, wrapped in it."
"7109","28 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Fazara narrating from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Maymuna, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her while lawful, and consummated with her while lawful, and she died at Sarif on the night he had consummated with her, and she was my maternal aunt, so I descended into her grave, I and Ibn Abbas. When we placed her in the lahd, her head inclined, so I took my cloak, folded it, and placed it under her head. Ibn Abbas pulled it and threw it away, and placed a cushion under her head. She said: And she had shaved during Hajj, and her head was hot."
"7110","29 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Maymuna, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me at Sarif, both of us lawful, after we returned from Makka."
"7111","30 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, he said: I said to al-Qasim: Shall I pray witr with three when the mu'adhdhin calls, then go out to prayer? He said: Do not pray except with five or seven. Al-Hakam said: I told that to Mujahid and Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, and they said to me: Ask him from whom is this? He said: From the trustworthy one, from A'isha and Maymuna, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7112","31 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymuna, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bathed and was brought a towel, but did not touch it, and kept gesturing with the water thus with his fingers, meaning shaking his hand."
"7113","32 - Zuhayr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj narrated to us, from Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard Maymuna say: I freed a slave girl in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I mentioned that to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: If you had given her to your maternal uncles, it would have been greater for your reward."
"7114","33 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Asamm narrated to us, from Yazid al-Asamm, he said: Maymuna, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), became gravely ill in Makka while none of her nephews were with her. She said: Take me out of Makka, for I will not die in it; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed me that I will not die in Makka. He said: So they carried her until they brought her to Sarif, to the tree under which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had consummated with her, at the site of the dome. He said: So she died, and when we placed her in her lahd, I took my cloak and placed it under her cheek in the lahd, and Ibn Abbas took it and threw it away."
"7115","34 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abbad narrated to us, from Hanzala al-Sadusi, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal say: Maymuna bint al-Harith, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rak'as before Asr."
"7116","35 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymuna bint al-Harith, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon us one day listless. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, why do I see you listless? He said: Gabriel, peace be upon him, promised to come to me, and he never broke his promise to me. She said: So he remained that day and night. She said: Then he suspected a puppy that was under their couch belonging to Husayn, so he ordered it to be taken out, and ordered water and sprinkled its place with his hand. He said: Then he went out and there was Gabriel, peace be upon them. He said: You promised to come to me. Gabriel, peace be upon him, said: We do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered dogs to be killed, until even the small walled-garden dog would be pleaded for, but he would not permit it."
"7117","36 - Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Nafi' narrating from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Ma'bad ibn Abbas, from Maymuna, that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque."
"7118","Hadith of Safiyya bint Huyayy ibn Akhtab, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), may Allah be pleased with her. 1 - Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Sulayman, meaning Ibn al-Mughira, narrated to us, Humayd, meaning Ibn Hilal, narrated to us that Safiyya said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while there was no one among people more hateful to me than him. He said: Your people did such and such. She said: I did not rise from my seat while there was no one among people more beloved to me than him."
"7119","2 - Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Ishaq al-Hashimi. Safiyya narrated to us, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me, so I offered him a cold shoulder, and I kept serving it to him; he ate it, then stood and prayed."
"7120","3 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salama, from Abu Idris, from Ibn Safwan, from Safiyya, Mother of the Believers, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will not cease raiding this House until an army raids it; when they are in a desert land, their first and last will be swallowed up, and their middle will not escape. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what about the coerced among them? He said: Allah Almighty will raise them according to what is in their hearts."
"7121","4 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Ya'la ibn Hakim narrating from Suhayra bint Jayfar, from Safiyya, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the nabidh of jars."
"7122","5 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Hashim al-Kufi narrated to us, Kinana narrated to us, he said: Safiyya narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made her manumission her dowry, and that he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her while in her hand were four thousand date-stones with which she glorified Allah. He said: I have glorified since I stood over you more than you have glorified. She said: I said: Teach me, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Say: Glory be to Allah as many as He created."
"7123","6 - Abu Hisham Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Rifa'a narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Mujammi', he said: Uthman ibn Ka'b narrated to me, from a man called Rabi', from Safiyya bint Huyayy, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mounted me behind him on the back of his she-camel at night. She said: I began to doze, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would touch me with his hand and say: O you, O daughter of Huyayy. And he kept saying: O Safiyya, I apologize to you for what I did to your people; they said to me such and such, they said to me such and such."
"7124","7 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Isma'il informed us, he said: Uthman ibn Ka'b narrated to me, he said: Rabi', a man of Banu al-Nadir who was in the care of Safiyya, narrated to me from Safiyya bint Huyayy, she said: I never saw anyone of better character than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I saw him mount me from Khaybar behind him on his she-camel at night; I began to doze and my head would strike the back of the saddle, so he would touch me with his hand and say: O you, gently, O daughter of Huyayy. Until when he came to al-Sahba, he said: I apologize to you, O Safiyya, for what I did to your people; they said to me such and such."
"7125","8 - Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, he said: Safiyya bint Huyayy, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to me, she said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and spoke with him while he was in retreat in the mosque. One night he stood with me to take me to my house, and two men of the Ansar met him. When they saw him, they felt shy and turned back. He said: Come here, for she is Safiyya, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They said: We seek refuge with Allah! Glory be to Allah! He said: I do not say this to you because you might think evil, but I know that Satan runs through the son of Adam as blood runs."
"7126","Hadith of Umm Habiba bint Abi Sufyan, Mother of the Believers. 1 - Abu Khaythama Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, Amr narrated to us, from Salim ibn Shawwal, from Umm Habiba, she said: We used to do it in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), meaning we prayed Fajr at Mina on the day of sacrifice."
"7127","2 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Yahya, from Humayd ibn Nafi', from Zaynab bint Abi Salama, from her mother Umm Salama and Umm Habiba, wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, my daughter's husband has died, and she is observing waiting, and I fear for her eye; shall I apply kohl to her? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One of your women used to throw a dung after a year, and it is only four months and ten days."
"7128","3 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, al-Nu'man ibn Salim informed us, from Amr ibn Aws, he said: Anbasa ibn Abi Sufyan said to me: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith narrated to us by Umm Habiba bint Abi Sufyan? He said: Yes indeed. He said: And what did you see? He said: That is only like glad tidings to you. He said: She narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays twelve voluntary prostrations in a day, a house will be built for him with them in Paradise. Umm Habiba said: I have not left them since I heard them. Al-Nu'man said: I have not left them since I heard them from Amr. Dawud said: As for us, we pray them and leave them."
"7129","4 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, he said: Nafi' informed me, from Salim, from Abu al-Jarrah, from Umm Habiba, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell."
"7130","5 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Suwayd ibn Qays, from Mu'awiya ibn Hudayj, from Mu'awiya ibn Abi Sufyan, that he asked his sister Umm Habiba, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray in the garment in which he had intercourse with her? She said: Yes, when he did not see any impurity in it."
"7131","6 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Talha narrated to me, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from Abu al-Jarrah, freedman of Umm Habiba, from Umm Habiba, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Were it not that I would burden my nation, I would command them to use the tooth-stick at every prayer, as they perform ablution."
"7132","7 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle, he said: Urwa ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Zaynab bint Umm Salama informed him that Umm Habiba, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed her, she said: O Messenger of Allah, marry my sister, the daughter of Abu Sufyan. She claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Do you like that? She said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah; I am not alone with you, and the one I most like to share good with me is my sister. She said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is not lawful for me. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, we talk that you want to marry Durra bint Abi Salama. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The daughter of Umm Salama? She said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, even if she were not my stepdaughter in my care, she would not be lawful for me; she is the daughter of my milk-brother; Thuwayba suckled me and Abu Salama. So do not offer me your daughters or your sisters."
"7133","8 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ali and Nafi' narrated to me that Amr ibn Nafi', freedman of Umar ibn al-Khattab, narrated to them that he used to write copies of the mushaf in the time of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Hafsa had me write a mushaf, and said to me: When you reach this verse of Surat al-Baqara, do not write it until you bring it to me, so I dictate it to you as I memorized it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: When I reached it, I brought her the sheet I was writing on, and she said: Write: Maintain the prayers and the middle prayer and the Asr prayer, and stand for Allah devoutly."
"7134","9 - Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Shu'aythi informed us, from his father, from Anbasa ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habiba, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays four before Zuhr and four after it, Allah will forbid him to the Fire."
"7135","10 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Habiba, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on a khumra."
"7136","11 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Khunays narrated to us, he said: We entered upon Sufyan al-Thawri visiting him for an illness he had, and Sa'id ibn Hassan al-Makhzumi entered upon us. Sufyan said to him: Repeat to me what you narrated to me from Umm Salih. He said: Sa'id said: Yes; Umm Salih narrated to me from Safiyya bint Shayba, from Umm Habiba, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All the speech of the son of Adam is against him, not for him, except commanding right, or forbidding wrong, or remembering Allah Almighty."
"7137","12 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Juwayriya narrated to us, from Nafi', that Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to him that al-Jarrah, freedman of Umm Habiba, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to Abdullah ibn Umar that Umm Habiba narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A caravan in which there is a bell will not be accompanied by the angels."
"7138","13 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Khunays al-Makki narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Hassan narrated to us, he said: Umm Salih narrated to me from Safiyya bint Shayba, from Umm Habiba, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All the speech of the son of Adam is against him, not for him, except commanding right, or forbidding wrong, or remembering Allah."
"7139","14 - Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Salim ibn Munqidh, from Amr ibn Aws al-Thaqafi, he said: I entered upon Anbasa ibn Abi Sufyan while he was dying, and he said: I do not like that you... and that is because I will narrate to you a hadith narrated to me by Umm Habiba bint Abi Sufyan; she narrated to me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays twelve rak'as along with the daytime prayer, Allah Almighty will build for him a house in Paradise."
"7140","15 - Shayban narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Nafi' narrated to us, from Salim, from al-Jarrah, freedman of Umm Habiba, from Umm Habiba, that she said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A company in which there is a bell will not be accompanied by the angels."
"7141","16 - Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Mu'adhdhin, from Abdullah ibn Anbasa, say: I heard Umm Habiba bint Abi Sufyan say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever maintains four rak'as before Asr, Allah Almighty will build for him a house in Paradise."
"7142","17 - Abu Nasr Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Qushayri al-Tammar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Umm Habiba, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays twelve rak'as in a day, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."
"7143","18 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Shu'aythi Abu Abdullah narrated to us, from his father, from Anbasa ibn Abi Sufyan, from his sister Umm Habiba, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: Whoever prays four rak'as before Zuhr and four after it, Allah Almighty will forbid him to the Fire."
"7144","19 - Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Ata al-Khurasani informed me, from Mu'awiya ibn Abi Sufyan, he said: I entered upon Umm Habiba, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing praying in a single garment with its ends crossed. I said: O Umm Habiba, does the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray in a single garment? She said: Yes, and it is the garment in which there was what was, meaning intercourse."
"7145","20 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Abu al-Malih ibn Usama, from Umm Habiba, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he heard the mu'adhdhin, he would say as the mu'adhdhin says until he falls silent."
"7146","21 - Bundar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman and Bahz narrated to me, from Shu'ba, from Abu Bishr, from Abu al-Malih, from Abdullah ibn Utba, from Umm Habiba, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said as the mu'adhdhin says until he falls silent."
"7147","22 - Rawh ibn Abd al-Mu'min al-Muqri narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd ibn Ibrahim al-Awfi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Talha ibn Yazid ibn Rukana, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from Abu al-Jarrah, freedman of Umm Habiba, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that Umm Habiba bint Abi Sufyan narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would burden my nation, I would command them to use the tooth-stick at every prayer, as they perform ablution."
"7148","23 - Abu Bakr ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, Abu Mushir narrated to us, he said: Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to me, al-Ala narrated to us, from Makhul, from Anbasa ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habiba, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution. Al-Ala said: Makhul said: Whoever touches it deliberately."
"7149","24 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salama, from Abu Sufyan ibn Sa'id, from Umm Habiba, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution because of what fire touched."
"7150","25 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Abu Malih, from Abdullah ibn Utba, from his paternal aunt Umm Habiba, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he heard the mu'adhdhin, would say as he says until he falls silent."
"7151","26 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Darraj narrated to us, from Umar ibn al-Hakam, that he narrated to him from Umm Habiba bint Abi Sufyan, that people of Yemen came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he taught them prayer, practices, and obligations. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we have a drink we make from wheat and barley? He said: Al-ghubayra? They said: Yes. He said: Do not taste it. Then after two days they mentioned it to him again. He said: Al-ghubayra? They said: Yes. He said: Do not taste it. Then when they wanted to leave, they asked him about it, and he said: Al-ghubayra? They said: Yes. He said: Do not taste it. They said: They will not leave it. He said: Whoever does not leave it, strike his neck."
"7152","Hadith of Umm Umara bint Ka'b, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 1 - Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, Shu'ba informed us, from Habib ibn Zayd al-Ansari, he said: I heard a freedwoman of ours called Layla narrating from Umm Umara bint Ka'b that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her, and she called for food for him. He said: Come and eat. She said: I am fasting. He said: When food is eaten in the presence of a fasting person, the angels pray for him."
"7153","Hadith of Umm Hisham bint Haritha ibn al-Nu'man from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 1 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Yahya ibn Abdullah, from Umm Hisham bint Haritha ibn al-Nu'man, she said: I recited Qaf and the Glorious Qur'an from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he used to recite it every Friday when he addressed the people."
"7154","2 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Shababa ibn Sawwar narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'n, from the daughter of Haritha ibn al-Nu'man, she said: Our oven and the oven of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were one. She said: So I memorized Qaf from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on Friday."
"7155","Hadith of Duba'a bint al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 1 - Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn al-Harith, that his grandmother Umm al-Hakam narrated to him from her sister Duba'a bint al-Zubayr that she offered meat to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ate from it, then prayed without performing ablution."
"7156","Hadith of the sister of Abdullah ibn Rawaha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 1 - Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'ba, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Nu'man narrated to me, from Talha ibn Musarrif, from a woman of Abd al-Qays, from the sister of Abdullah ibn Rawaha, she said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Going out is obligatory upon every woman with a waistband, meaning in the two Eids."
"7157","Hadith of a woman, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 1 - Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Abi Abdullah, from Budayl ibn Maysara, from Abdullah ibn Utba, from a woman, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a skin of milk, and a Bedouin took it in three morsels. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had he said: In the name of Allah, it would have sufficed you. And he said: When one of you forgets the name of Allah over his food, let him say when he remembers: In the name of Allah, at its beginning and end."
"7158","Hadith of Zaynab bint Jahsh, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 1 - Harun ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, he said: Salih, freedman of al-Taw'ama, narrated to me from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to women in the year of the Farewell Hajj: This, then the backs of mats. He said: So all of them performed Hajj except Sawda bint Zam'a and Zaynab bint Jahsh, for they would say: By Allah, no mount will move us after we heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7159","2 - Ishaq and Harun al-Hammal narrated to us, and the wording is Ishaq's, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Zaynab, from Habiba, from Umm Habiba, from Zaynab, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke from sleep with his face red, saying: There is no god but Allah! Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near; today there has been opened of the barrier of Gog and Magog like this. Zaynab said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we perish while the righteous are among us? He said: Yes, when filth increases."
"7160","3 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Mansur ibn Salama al-Khuza'i narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Humayd ibn Nafi', from Zaynab bint Umm Salama, that she informed him, she said: I entered upon Zaynab bint Jahsh when her brother died, and she called for perfume and touched some of it, then said: By Allah, I have no need of perfume, except that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say on the pulpit: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead person for more than three nights, except over a husband, four months and ten days."
"7161","4 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid al-Hanafi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Zaynab bint Jahsh, that she used to comb the hair of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a brass basin."
"7162","5 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Salih, freedman of al-Taw'ama, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his wives: This Hajj, then the backs of mats. All of them performed Hajj except Zaynab and Sawda; they said: No mount will move us after the word of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), meaning: This, then the backs of mats."
"7163","6 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Zaynab, from Habiba, from Umm Habiba, from Zaynab, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke from sleep with his face red, saying: There is no god but Allah; woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near; today there has been opened of the barrier of Gog and Magog like this. Zaynab said: Shall we perish while the righteous are among us? He said: Yes, when filth increases."
"7164","Hadith of Razina. 1 - Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Ulayla bint al-Kumayt narrated to us, she said: My mother Amina narrated to me that Amatullah bint Razina narrated to her from her mother Razina, freedwoman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that Sawda the Yemeni came to visit A'isha, while Hafsa bint Umar was with her. Sawda came in fine dress and condition, wearing a Yemeni cloak and a similar head-cover, with two lentil-like spots of aloes and saffron at her temples. Ulayla said: And I knew women adorning themselves with it. Hafsa said to A'isha: O Mother of the Believers, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will come reluctantly while this one shines among us? The Mother of the Believers said to her: Fear Allah, O Hafsa; fear Allah, O Hafsa. She said: I will spoil her adornment. She said: What are you saying? And she was hard of hearing. Hafsa said to her: O Sawda, the one-eyed one has come out. She said: Really? She was terribly frightened and began to tremble. She said: Where shall I hide? She said: To the tent, a tent of theirs of palm leaves in which they cooked. She went and hid in it, in which were filth and spider webs. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while the two were laughing, unable to speak from laughter. He said: What is this laughter? Three times. They gestured with their hands to the tent. He went and found Sawda trembling. He said to her: O Sawda, what is wrong with you? She said: O Messenger of Allah, the one-eyed one has come out. He said: He has not come out, but he will surely come out; he has not come out, but he will surely come out; he has not come out, but he will surely come out. Then he entered and brought her out, brushing dust and spider webs from her."
"7165","2 - Abu Sa'id al-Jushami narrated to us, he said: Ulayla bint al-Kumayt narrated to us, she said: I heard my mother Amina say: Amatullah bint Razina narrated to me from her mother Razina, freedwoman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he took Safiyya captive on the day of Qurayza and al-Nadir when Allah granted him victory, and brought her leading her as a captive. When she saw the women, she said: I testify that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah. So he released her, while her arm was in his hand, then freed her, proposed to her, married her, and gave her a dowry."
"7166","3 - Ubaydullah al-Qawariri narrated to us, Ulayla narrated to us, from her mother, she said: I said to Amatullah bint Razina: O Amatullah, did your mother Razina narrate to you that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention the fast of Ashura? She said: Yes, and he used to honor it so much that he would call his nursing infants and the nursing infants of his daughter Fatima, spit in their mouths, and say to the mothers: Do not nurse them until night."
"7167","Hadith of Halima bint al-Harith, mother of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 1 - Masruq ibn al-Marzuban al-Kufi and al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated to us, and I copied it from the hadith of Masruq, Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Za'ida narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Jahm ibn Abi Jahm, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, from Halima bint al-Harith, mother of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), al-Sa'diyya who nursed him, she said: I went out among women of Banu Sa'd ibn Bakr seeking nursing infants in Makka, upon a grey she-donkey of mine that had grown weak, crowding with the caravan. She said: We went out in a barren year that left nothing, with my husband al-Harith ibn Abd al-Uzza. She said: With us was an old she-camel of ours that would not yield a drop of milk, and with me was a boy of mine; we could not sleep our night with his crying, for my breast had nothing to suffice him, and our old camel had no milk to feed him, except that we hoped. When we reached Makka, every woman among us was offered the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and refused him, for we hoped for generous nursing payment from the father of the child, and he was an orphan, so we said: What could his mother do? Until no woman of my companions remained but took a boy other than me, and I disliked returning without taking anything while my companions had taken. I said to my husband: By Allah, I will return to that one and take him. She said: So I came to him, took him, and brought him to my dwelling. My husband said: Have you taken him? I said: Yes, by Allah, since I found no other. He said: You did right; perhaps Allah will place good in him. She said: By Allah, as soon as I placed him in my lap, my breast flowed with milk for him as He willed. She said: He drank until satisfied, and his brother, meaning her son, drank until satisfied, and my husband went to our old camel at night and found it full, so he milked for us as we wished, and he drank until satisfied. She said: And I drank until satisfied. We spent that night in good, full and quenched, and our boys slept. She said: His father, meaning her husband, said: By Allah, O Halima, I think you have taken a blessed soul; our boy has slept and is satisfied. She said: Then we left, and by Allah, my she-donkey went ahead of the caravan and outstripped them so they could not reach her, so they said: Woe to you, O daughter of al-Harith, hold back for us; is this not your donkey you left upon? I said: Yes, by Allah, and she is ahead of us, until we reached our dwellings among Banu Sa'd ibn Bakr, arriving upon the most barren land of Allah. By Him in whose hand is Halima's soul, they would send out their sheep in the morning, and my shepherd would go out, and my sheep would return with full bellies, milky and udder-full, while their sheep returned hungry and perishing, with no milk. She said: We drank milk as we wished, while no one in the settlement milked a drop or found it. They said to their shepherds: Woe to you, do you not pasture where Halima's shepherd pastures? They would pasture in the valley where our shepherd pastured, yet their sheep returned hungry with no milk, while my sheep returned milky and full. She said: He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would grow in a day as a boy grows in a month, and grow in a month as a boy grows in a year, until he reached six as a sturdy boy. She said: We came to his mother, and we said to her, and his father said to her: Return our son to us; let us return with him, for we fear the epidemic of Makka for him. She said: While we clung to him most for the blessing we had seen. She said: He kept at her until she said: Return with him. So we returned with him, and he stayed with us two months. She said: While he was playing with his brother one day behind the houses, grazing our lambs, his brother came to us running and said to me and his father: Reach my Qurayshi brother; two men came to him, laid him down, and split his belly. We rushed toward him and found him standing with changed color. His father embraced him and I embraced him, then we said: What is wrong with you, my son? He said: Two men in white clothes came to me, laid me down, then split my belly; by Allah, I do not know what they did. She said: We carried him and returned with him. She said: His father said: By Allah, O Halima, I think this boy has been struck; let us return him to his family before what we fear appears. She said: We returned him to her, and she said: What brought you back with him when you were keen upon him? She said: I said: By Allah, only that we reared him and fulfilled our duty toward him, then I feared events for him, so we said he should be among his family. She said: Amina said: By Allah, that is not your case; tell me your story and his. By Allah, she kept at us until we told her his story. She said: Did you fear for him? No, by Allah; this son of mine has a great matter. Shall I not tell you about him? I carried him, and never carried a load lighter or more blessed than him. Then I saw a light like a shooting star coming from me when I bore him, lighting for me the necks of camels in Busra. Then I bore him, and he did not fall as boys fall: he fell placing his hand on the ground, raising his head to the sky. Leave him and attend to your own affair."
"7168","Musnad of Tamim al-Dari. 1 - Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Tamim al-Dari, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Religion is only sincere advice; religion is only sincere advice; religion is only sincere advice. They said: To whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: To Allah, His Messenger, His Book, the leaders of the Muslims and their common folk."
"7169","2 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Abdullah ibn Mawhab, from Tamim al-Dari, he said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a man who embraces Islam at the hands of a man. He said: He is most entitled to him in his life and death."
"7170","1 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, from Abdullah ibn Rabah, from a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Asr, then a man stood praying. Umar saw him and said to him: Sit, for the People of the Book perished only because their prayers had no separation. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ibn al-Khattab did well."
"7171","1 - Muhammad ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, al-Juddi narrated to us, Shu'ba informed us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I heard my uncle narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever hears the call on Friday and does not come, or does not answer, then hears the call and does not come, or does not answer, then hears the call and does not come, or does not answer, Allah Almighty will seal his heart and make it the heart of a hypocrite."
"7172","1 - Muhammad ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, al-Juddi narrated to us, Shu'ba informed us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban narrating from a man of the Ansar, from a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Three are a duty upon every Muslim on Friday: the tooth-stick, bathing, and perfume if available."
"7173","Hadith of Abu Wahb al-Jushami. 1 - Harun ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sa'id al-Talqani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muhajir al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Aqil ibn Shabib narrated to me from Abu Wahb al-Jushami, and he had companionship, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Name yourselves with the names of the prophets; the most beloved names to Allah are Abdullah and Abd al-Rahman; the truest are Harith and Hammam; and the ugliest are Harb and Murra."
"7174","2 - With his chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep horses, wipe their forelocks and rumps, or he said their backs, girth them, and do not bridle them with strings."
"7175","3 - With his chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep to every dark-bay with a blaze and white feet, or black with a blaze and white feet."
"7176","Musnad of Usayd ibn Zuhayr. 1 - Harun ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far al-Ansari narrated to me, Abu al-Abrad, freedman of Banu Khatma, narrated to us that he heard Usayd ibn Zuhayr al-Ansari, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A prayer in the mosque of Quba is like an Umra."
"7177","Hadith of al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wada'a al-Sahmi. 1 - Harun al-Hammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Kathir ibn al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wada'a narrated to us, from some of his family, he said: I heard al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wada'a al-Sahmi say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying toward the door of Banu Sahm, while people passed in front of him, with no screen between him and the qibla."
"7178","Hadith of Amr ibn Hazm. 1 - al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq ibn Asma al-Jarmi narrated to us, Ja'far narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: When Mu'awiya wanted to appoint Yazid as successor, he sent to the governor of Madina to send to him whom he wished. He said: Amr ibn Hazm al-Ansari came to him as a delegate, and sought permission. The chamberlain of Mu'awiya came seeking permission and said: This is Amr who has come seeking permission. He said: What brought them to me? He said: O Commander of the Believers, he has come seeking your bounty. Mu'awiya said: If you are truthful, let him write what he wishes, and give him what he asks you, and do not let me see him. He said: The chamberlain went out to him and said: What is your need? Write what you wish. He said: Glory be to Allah! Shall I come to the door of the Commander of the Believers and be veiled from him? I wish to meet him and speak to him. Mu'awiya said to the chamberlain: Promise him such and such day, when he prays the morning prayer, let him come. He said: When Mu'awiya prayed the morning prayer, he ordered a couch to be placed in his hall, then cleared people from him, and there was no one with him except a chair placed for Amr. Amr came, sought permission, was permitted, greeted him, then sat on the chair. Mu'awiya said to him: Your need. He said: He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: By my life, Yazid ibn Mu'awiya has become of middle lineage in Quraysh, rich beyond money, in need of nothing but all good, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah has not entrusted a servant with subjects except that He will question him about them on the Day of Resurrection, how he acted toward them. And I remind you of Allah, O Mu'awiya, concerning the nation of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whom you appoint over them. He said: Mu'awiya was seized with panting and breathing on a cold morning until he sweated, wiping sweat from his face three times, then recovered, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: As for what follows, you are a sincere man; you spoke your opinion, far-reaching as it is, and there remain only my son and their sons, and my son is more entitled than their sons. Your need. He said: I have no need. He said: Then his brother said to him: Did we come from Madina exhausting camels for mere words? He said: I came only for words. He said: So he ordered gifts for them. He said: And the like came out for Amr."
"7179","2 - Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ar'ara narrated to us, and his copy is from the copy of Ibrahim, they said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ibn Tawus, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from his father, he said: Amr ibn Hazm entered upon Amr ibn al-As and said: Ammar has been killed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The rebellious party will kill him. Then Amr entered upon Mu'awiya and said: Ammar has been killed. Mu'awiya said: Ammar has been killed, so what? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The rebellious party will kill him. He said: You have slipped in your urine; did we kill him? Only Ali and his companions killed him."
"7180","3 - Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm narrated to me, he said: I presented to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the ruqya for a snake bite, and he commanded it."
"7181","Report of Buhaysah from her father (7177): Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, Kahmas ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Sayyar, a man of Banu Fazara, from his father, from Buhaysah, from her father, who said: My father sought permission of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), entered behind him between him and his shirt from the back, embraced him, and kept saying: O Prophet of Allah, what is the thing it is not lawful to withhold? He said: Water. He said: O Prophet of Allah, what is the thing it is not lawful to withhold? He said: Salt. He said: O Prophet of Allah, what is the thing it is not lawful to withhold? He said: To do good is better for you. He said: So he held to water and salt. That man never withheld anything of water, even if little."
"7182","Report of Razin ibn Anas al-Sulami (7178): Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Wail Khalid ibn Muhammad al-Basri narrated to us, Fahd ibn Awf narrated to us at Banu Amir's dwelling, Nail ibn Mutarrif ibn Razin ibn Anas al-Sulami narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me from my grandfather Razin ibn Anas, who said: When Islam appeared we had a well, and I feared those around it would overpower us over it, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we have a well and I fear those around it will overpower us over it. So he wrote for me a document: From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah; as for what follows: they shall have their well, if he is truthful, and they shall have their house, if he is truthful. He said: We never presented it to any judge of Madinah but they judged for us by it. And in the letter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the spelling of kana was kawun."
"7183","Report of a man of Balqayn (7179): Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Budayl ibn Maysarah, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from a man of Balqayn, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at Wadi al-Qura, and said: O Messenger of Allah, what have you been commanded? He said: I have been commanded that you worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, establish prayer, and give zakat. I said: O Messenger of Allah, who are these? He said: Those who earned anger, meaning the Jews. I said: Who are these? He said: Those astray, meaning the Christians. I said: To whom belongs the spoils, O Messenger of Allah? He said: To Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is one share, and to these are four shares. I said: Is anyone more entitled to the spoils than another? He said: No; even the arrow one of you takes from his quiver, he is not more entitled to it than anyone."
"7184","Report of al-Miswar ibn Makhramah (7180): Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Asim ibn Umar, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, who said: Subay’ah gave birth a few days after her husband’s death, came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), sought his permission to marry, and he permitted her."
"7185","(7181): Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Abi Mani’ al-Rusafi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, that Ali ibn Husayn informed him that al-Miswar ibn Makhramah informed him that Ali proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl; that reached Fatimah, so she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: People claim you do not become angry for your daughters, and here Ali is marrying the daughter of Abu Jahl. Al-Miswar said: I witnessed him when he bore witness, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: As for what follows: I married my daughter to Abu al-As, he spoke to me and told me the truth; Fatimah is but a part of me, and by Allah the daughter of the Messenger of Allah and the daughter of the enemy of Allah shall never be joined with one Muslim man ever. So Ali withdrew from the proposal."
"7186","(7182): al-Dawraqi Abu Abd Allah Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Mubashshir narrated to us, from al-Awza’i, from al-Zuhri, I think he said: Ali ibn Husayn informed me that Ibn Abbas said: A man of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the Ansar informed me that while they were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a star was shot and it lit up, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: What did you used to say in the pre-Islamic era when the like of this was shot? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best; we used to say: Tonight a great man is born, and tonight a great man dies. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not shot for anyone’s death nor for his life, but when our Lord, Mighty and Majestic, decrees a matter the bearers of the Throne glorify, then the people of heaven next to them glorify, until the glorification reaches the people of the heaven next to them, then they say to those next to them, the bearers of the Throne: What did your Lord say? They inform them, and the people of the heavens ask one another until the news reaches the people of the lowest heaven, then the jinn snatch the hearing and cast it to their allies, and they are shot; what they bring as it is, is true, but they mix falsehood with it, or add to it. The doubt is from Mubashshir."
"7187","Report of Khalid ibn al-Walid (7183): Surayj ibn Yunus Abu al-Harith narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja’far, from his father, who said: Khalid ibn al-Walid said: We performed Umrah with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in an Umrah he performed, so he shaved his hair, people raced to his hair, I raced to the forelock and took it, made a cap and placed it at the front of the cap, and I was never directed to any front but it was opened for me."
"7188","(7184): Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Shaybah ibn al-Ahnaf, who heard Abu Sallam al-Aswad saying: Abu Salih al-Ash’ari informed me that Abu Abd Allah al-Ash’ari narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying not completing his bowing nor his prostration, and said: If this one died upon what he is upon, he would die upon other than the religion of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So complete the bowing and prostration, for the likeness of one who does not complete his bowing nor his prostration is like the hungry one who eats only one date or two dates, they avail him nothing. Abu Salih said: I met Abu Abd Allah and said: Who narrated this hadith to you that he heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: The commanders of the armies narrated it to me: Khalid ibn al-Walid, Shurahbil ibn Hasanah, and Amr ibn al-As, that they heard it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7189","(7185): Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Isma’il, from Qays, who said: Khalid ibn al-Walid said: No night in which a bride is brought to my house whom I love, or in which I am given glad tidings of a boy, is dearer to me than a severely cold night in a detachment of the Emigrants with which I attack the enemy at dawn."
"7190","(7186): Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Abu al-Safar, who said: Khalid ibn al-Walid camped at al-Hirah under the authority of Banu al-Marazibah, and they said to him: Beware of poison, lest the non-Arabs give you to drink. He said: Bring it to me. It was brought, he took it in his hand, then swallowed it and said: In the name of Allah. It did not harm him at all."
"7191","(7187): Surayj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Isma’il, from Qays, who said: I heard Khalid ibn al-Walid narrating to the people in al-Jaridah, saying: I saw myself on the day of Mu’tah, nine swords broke in my hands, and a Yemeni plate of mine remained with me."
"7192","(7188): Surayj narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, saying: Isma’il narrated to me, from Qays, who said: Khalid ibn al-Walid said: Striving in the path of Allah has kept me from much recitation."
"7193","(7188) repeated, with the same chain from Qays, who said: I was informed that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile Khalid, for he is a sword of the swords of Allah, which Allah drew against the disbelievers."
"7194","(7189): Abu al-Harith narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, saying: Isma’il narrated to me, from Qays, who said: I saw Khalid ibn al-Walid leading the people in the army in a single garment."
"7195","(7190): Abu al-Harith Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za’idah narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us, from Amir, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away and those who apostatized apostatized, some people said: We shall pray but not give zakat. People said to Abu Bakr: Accept it from them. He said: If they withheld from me a young goat I would fight them. So he sent Khalid ibn al-Walid, and Adi ibn Hatim came with a thousand men of Tayyi’ until he reached al-Yamamah. Banu Amir had killed the workers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and burned them with fire. So Abu Bakr wrote to Khalid: Kill Banu Amir and burn them with fire. He did so until the women cried out. Then he marched until he reached the water; they came out to him saying: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, we bear witness there is no god but Allah, we bear witness Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. When he heard that he held back from them. Then Abu Bakr ordered him to march until he camped at al-Hirah, then proceed to Syria. When he camped at al-Hirah he wrote to the people of Persia, then said: I love not to depart until I frighten them. So he raided them until he reached Sura, killed and took captives, then raided Ayn al-Tamr, killed and took captives, then proceeded to Syria. Amir said: Ibn Buqaylah brought out to me Khalid’s letter: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate; from Khalid ibn al-Walid to the chiefs of the people of Persia: Peace upon whoever follows guidance. I praise Allah, besides whom there is no god, with the praise by which He split your sanctities, divided your unity, weakened your might, and stripped your kingdom. When this letter of mine reaches you, accept protection from me, pay the jizyah to me, and send hostages to me; otherwise, by the One besides whom there is no god, I shall meet you with a people who love death as you love life. Peace upon whoever follows guidance."
"7196","(7191): Abu Hammam narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, saying: Safwan narrated to me. Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to me, from his father, from Khalid ibn al-Walid, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not take a fifth from the salab."
"7197","(7192): Abu Hammam narrated to us, saying: Isma’il narrated to me, from Safwan ibn Amr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Khalid ibn al-Walid, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not take a fifth from the salab."
"7198","Report of Amir ibn Rabi’ah (7193): Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm al-Antaki narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak informed us, Sufyan al-Thawri informed us, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Asim ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi’ah, from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) using the siwak while fasting, more times than I can count, or he said: than I can enumerate."
"7199","(7194): Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Jushami narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa’id and Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Shu’bah, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi’ah narrating from his father that a woman of Banu Fazarah married a man for two sandals, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her, in Yahya’s narration: Are you content with these two sandals for yourself and your wealth? And in Abd al-Rahman’s narration: Are you content with two sandals for himself and his wealth? She said: Yes. So he permitted it."
"7200","(7195): Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Isa, from Umayyah ibn Hind, from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi’ah, from his father, who said: I set out with Sahl ibn Hunayf seeking a secluded place; we found a secluded spot and a pond, and each of us was shy to bathe while anyone saw him, so he screened himself from me, removed a cloak over him, then entered the water. I looked at him and struck him with the evil eye from it. I called him and he did not answer me, so I informed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He came to him, struck his chest, then said: O Allah, remove its heat, its cold, and its ailment. Then he said: Stand. So he stood. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you sees in himself, his wealth, or his brother what pleases him, let him supplicate for blessing, for the evil eye is true."
